{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation","id":97188,"title":"Are lunars the best philosophers in creation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-23T19:12:05-07:00","id":97188,"title":"Are lunars the best philosophers in creation?","content":"Considering the fact that their splat is based around abilities, lunar should in theory be the best at abstract thinking. thing like philosohpy and riddles should be thing they excel at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T19:15:47-07:00","id":97192,"title":"","content":"They're based on Attributes, not Abilities.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'm not sure. You have a small point, but I think Solars could get higher dice pools for it, so that kinda makes them better regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T19:40:34-07:00","id":97218,"title":"","content":"Philosophy and Riddles are not raw applications of intelligence A Solar who specializes in the appropriate ability (likely Lore) is going to be at least as capable.<br /> <br /> In general, even for things that *are* directly linked to soley attribute or an ability, both kinds of exalts (ability/attribute based, not just Solar/Lunar) are likely to have charms that work for them. Solars have soak boosting charms in Resistance, despite Resistance not normally adding to soak (only STA would). Lunars have charms to speak other languages, despite languages being solely a function of Linguistics, with no normally applicable attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T19:52:14-07:00","id":97224,"title":"","content":"And no Exalted have Charms based on Virtues, but there are those pesky Charms in Integrity and Charisma...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:00:56-07:00","id":97225,"title":"","content":"I don't know of any splat that has charms that specifically enhance talking about metaphysics or morality. I hope no splat ever does get those, because a philosophy degree is basically useless and I can't imagine philosophy charms would be much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 03-23-2014, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:04:57-07:00","id":97229,"title":"","content":"Hmm, not wrong. Lunar are the most flexible of all Exalts, which'd give them an advantage in thinking in new ways, which philosophy and riddles can require.<br /> <br /> Problem is, the Solar are granted the gift of perfection, which allows them to be the best at everything. Now, there's a lot of areas this can be argued, but cleverness doesn't really seem to be one?<br /> <br /> I suppose if you mechanicalise it, Lunar have Intelligence Charms, while Solar only have Lore/Occult/etc Charms, which'd only apply some of the time.<br /> <br /> Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:45:45-07:00","id":97254,"title":"","content":"How, exactly, are you going to do the philosopher? No, I'm serious about this question, it isn't a trick.<br /> <br /> How do you want to represent it? Purely off of mental stats? Off of mental stats and Skills, or off of Skills alone?<br /> <br /> Or do you want this to be a more abstract thing, because out of those three options, none of them favor Lunars over Solars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T21:03:11-07:00","id":97274,"title":"","content":"Well, it's true that the Lunar Exalted are the only Exalts actually doing any evidence-based philosophical research at the moment... which is kind of amusing when you think about it.<br /> <br /> Earlier today, a Lunar NPC in my game was trying to explain to a Solar PC why he shouldn't rush in and save a Haslanti town from a Wyld-related disaster, arguing that it's best to let them save themselves if they can; even though it's cruel, ultimately Exalts have a duty to set emotion aside and do what's best for humanity and not for individuals. I don't think the Solar's going to listen, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-24-2014, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T21:13:38-07:00","id":97283,"title":"","content":"Pound for intellectual pound, I think that among the celestial Exalted, Lunars would actually be in second place with regards to philosophy. The title of &quot;best&quot; would be a hotly contested issue between the Solars (because of solar perfection and general Solarness) and the Sidereals (because of their connection to Fate and all the weird esoteric shenanigans they deal with regularly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T21:30:33-07:00","id":97292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97225#post97225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know of any splat that has charms that specifically enhance talking about metaphysics or morality. I hope no splat ever does get those, because a philosophy degree is basically useless and I can't imagine philosophy charms would be much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those of us with Philosophy degrees would tend to think otherwise. That said, I can at the very least see an Exigent that had a lot of charms based on philosophical shout outs like Xeno's Paradox of Motion to prevent the enemy from getting closer or Liminals using some sort of Ship of Theseus charm to draw on the magic of parts they don't currently have. The point shouldn't be about solving the &quot;big questions&quot; but approaching situations in new ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T01:14:03-07:00","id":97358,"title":"","content":"When we talk about great philosophers, we usually mean those who have brought something new to the table at a culturally appropriate time.<br /> <br /> It's not simply about being smart or thoughtful. It's about presenting an idea that captures the imagination of your contemporaries. I'd say Solars, not because they're the smartest, but because they can convince the most people to listen to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T01:49:48-07:00","id":97377,"title":"","content":"Ahahahahaha, AHAHAHAHAHA... No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97292#post97292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those of us with Philosophy degrees would tend to think otherwise. That said, I can at the very least see an Exigent that had a lot of charms based on philosophical shout outs like Xeno's Paradox of Motion to prevent the enemy from getting closer or Liminals using some sort of Ship of Theseus charm to draw on the magic of parts they don't currently have. The point shouldn't be about solving the &quot;big questions&quot; but approaching situations in new ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, As would anybody with even surface level interest in philosophy tell you, philosophy isn't about &quot;solving&quot; anything. It's about asking the right questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-24-2014, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T01:59:59-07:00","id":97381,"title":"","content":"Why are you telling someone with a philosophy degree that they don't even have a surface level interest in philosophy?<br /> <br /> Also, 'what is philosophy about?' is a philosophical question. Your response suggests you believe you've solved it, which makes your statement contradictory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:09:24-07:00","id":97384,"title":"","content":"Lunars being based on Attributes does not mean that Lunars are about being the best at those Attributes, not least because &quot;being the best at something&quot; is not one of the informative motifs of Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:10:35-07:00","id":97385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97381#post97381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you telling someone with a philosophy degree that they don't even have a surface level interest in philosophy?<br /> <br /> Also, 'what is philosophy about?' is a philosophical question. Your response suggests you believe you've solved it, which makes your statement contradictory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry, that looked bad. I meant to say it to everyone and my sentance was supposed to be a followup. But I can see that it wans't the best thing to do.<br /> <br /> Also, I like me some contradictions, contradictions are fun. Mostly when you spot them, when you don't they're just dangerous. But when you can see them they're so much fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:13:18-07:00","id":97387,"title":"","content":"Philosophy feels like one of those things where the qualities are so abstract and subjective that pretty much anybody can get in on it. There absolutely should have been First Age Exalts who swore by philosophical tracts composed by mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:24:06-07:00","id":97397,"title":"","content":"Within the cultural and social context of Creation, anyone recognized in-setting as a philosopher would also partake of what we would recognize as early forms of science, with all the broadness of the term - &quot;philosophers&quot; would be physicians and physicists, chemists and alchemists, sociologists and historians, teachers and advisors to kings. Philosophers would be widely respected as men of many useful skills as well as the kind of people who give you guidance in how to live your life, and you would rarely ever see people disparage philosophy as a fool's errand or pointless navel-gazing the way we modern people are used to.<br /> <br /> (&quot;rarely ever&quot; does not mean &quot;not ever,&quot; though: Aristophanes' caricature of Socrates was scathing, but that's what Aristophanes does)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 03-24-2014, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:27:24-07:00","id":97398,"title":"","content":"Sure, but we're not people in Creation. We're people on Earth in 2014 talking about who would make the best philosopher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:35:13-07:00","id":97404,"title":"","content":"And?<br /> <br /> The setting isn't going to provide you with a convenient modern-day philosopher slotted in among all the Iron Age-style philosophers that actually make sense for the setting.<br /> <br /> If you want the &quot;best&quot; philosopher in Creation, you're either going to take scientist-philosopher-viziers and stripping out all the &quot;non-philosophy&quot; parts of their work/life to evaluate the meaning of their &quot;purely philosophical&quot; work, at which point your result is nonsensical,* or you're going to have to evaluate how studying maths or the nature of atoms factors in the quality of your philosophy, at which point your result is nonsensical.<br /> <br /> Who is the best philosopher, Anaximander or Pythagoras? Or are they mathematicians? Or both?<br /> <br /> *mind, that's what a lot of modern study of philosophy tries to do anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 03-24-2014, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T04:33:49-07:00","id":97449,"title":"","content":"What does &quot;best&quot; mean in this context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T05:49:27-07:00","id":97466,"title":"","content":"Yes, from their own perspective. No, from someone else's. In other words, both and neither. So are you a Lunar?<br /> <br /> Edit: Answering a question with a question addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 03-24-2014, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T06:53:17-07:00","id":97492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97397#post97397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the cultural and social context of Creation, anyone recognized in-setting as a philosopher would also partake of what we would recognize as early forms of science, with all the broadness of the term - &quot;philosophers&quot; would be physicians and physicists, chemists and alchemists, sociologists and historians, teachers and advisors to kings. Philosophers would be widely respected as men of many useful skills as well as the kind of people who give you guidance in how to live your life, and you would rarely ever see people disparage philosophy as a fool's errand or pointless navel-gazing the way we modern people are used to.<br /> <br /> (&quot;rarely ever&quot; does not mean &quot;not ever,&quot; though: Aristophanes' caricature of Socrates was scathing, but that's what Aristophanes does)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're going by the Greek concept of philosophy, which is the search for how to &quot;live well&quot; (or the study of <i>eudaimonia,</i> &quot;human flourishing&quot;), I don't really see Lunars having any competition in the 2nd Edition setting. Even the crazy ones like Ma-Ha-Suchi are described as having philosophical motivations, opposing civilization on the grounds that it is a &quot;pernicious lie&quot; and ultimately not a good way of &quot;living well&quot;. Of the sane ones, most seem to be spending the majority of their time in actual philosophical research, testing different cultures specifically to identify ways of &quot;living well&quot;. That's why I said it was amusing, earlier. In 2nd Edition, the Silver Pact is presented as this big philosophy club with different schools of thought, or alternatively as a sociological journal. Which is kind of silly. But I don't really see that in any of the other Exalted at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T10:41:03-07:00","id":97603,"title":"","content":"Am I remembering correctly if I say that there is a philosophy school in Nexus and a philosophy... club... in Whitewall?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T10:49:45-07:00","id":97606,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to imagine how you would even tell who the best philosophers are. Is it, like, &quot;which philosopher is favoured in a white-room debate?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T10:54:17-07:00","id":97608,"title":"","content":"If my high school system is to be believed, you come up with a cleverly worded sentence (possibly including a &quot;pun&quot;) and give high school students 6 hours to write 4 to 16 pages attempting to answer it with their feeble memories of philosophy classes.<br /> <br /> Thesis-Antithesis-Synthesis, <i>motherfuckers!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T11:32:28-07:00","id":97635,"title":"","content":"In the ancient world (which Exalted is based on) philosophy encompassed natural science and the study of society. In other words, a Zenith, Twilight or Eclipse might be called a philosopher-king if they focus on applying a moral or natural philosophy to their subjects and their own rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T11:44:52-07:00","id":97640,"title":"","content":"To comment on the actual question: No I do not think Lunars make philosophers for the same reason that no one else does, its too important to the setting that no one has a strong handle on it.<br /> <br /> As Holden has said, there is no magic to rule with grace and wisdom. There is no charm to make a perfect world even though there are charms to create worlds. The questions about what Creation should look like and what the place of anything in it should be are ones everyone has to try to answer for themselves. Just because the Solar's utopian vision would be very shiny does not make it a good thing or better then the Sidereal's safe, stable, and soul-crushing plan. They have to settle it with their fists or with their after effects, and everything will constantly be in motion as they attempt to deal with each other. No easy answers to be found.<br /> <br /> At best, charms should make you better at picking holes in other people's ideas by improving your ability to consider consequences and structural problems. Those same charms would also make you better at refuting the flaws you or others find and to prop up a bad system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T11:58:34-07:00","id":97646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97384#post97384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars being based on Attributes does not mean that Lunars are about being the best at those Attributes, not least because &quot;being the best at something&quot; is not one of the informative motifs of Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is that, too. They're not &quot;the best&quot;, but rather, for a lack of better term, werewolves. So, while you can have Lunars that are Whywolves, that isn't working through the concept of being &quot;the best&quot; at rational inquiry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T12:14:10-07:00","id":97653,"title":"","content":"The main flaw in my argument is the fact that solars are meant to be the best at everything they want to excel at.<br /> <br /> Beyond that the the monster theme lunars have must be able to apply to social and intelectual characters as well, and having intelegence enhancing charms should make them better at abtract reasoning, which should (although i think its now the case) be a purely intelectual endeavor, not based on any ability.<br /> <br /> A many tongued hypnotic gazing seductress could be a monster as a social predator. a giantic brained character could be an intelectual monster. or someone who extends his brain through his body, like ultimate tony stark or an elastic brain like ultimate reed richards. the hulks enemy, the leader, could also be an example of a big brained super smart character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T12:17:11-07:00","id":97655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97646#post97646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is that, too. They're not &quot;the best&quot;, but rather, for a lack of better term, werewolves. So, while you can have Lunars that are Whywolves, that isn't working through the concept of being &quot;the best&quot; at rational inquiry.</div> </div> </div> </div>You beating Isator to Whywolves compariosn is so deliciously ironic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T13:03:29-07:00","id":97686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97653#post97653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beyond that the the monster theme lunars have must be able to apply to social and intelectual characters as well, and having intelegence enhancing charms should make them better at abtract reasoning, which should (although i think its now the case) be a purely intelectual endeavor, not based on any ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would that actually amount to in play?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a giantic brained character could be an intelectual monster. or someone who extends his brain through his body, like ultimate tony stark or an elastic brain like ultimate reed richards. the hulks enemy, the leader, could also be an example of a big brained super smart character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Big mutant brains doesn't really fit the Lunar motif. They don't need it for their Excellency (assuming they have one), they've got the advantage of divinity.<br /> <br /> I expect Lunar Intelligence Charms will be less warping the brain to enhance mental functions and more the Lunar rubric applied to mental purposes.<br /> <br /> It's like, when Sidereals had Brawl Charms, maybe there was some stuff like &quot;manipulate fate to land better punches&quot;, but it didn't stand out as much as &quot;punch an unfavourable future into something, and force them to choose between letting it happen or taking aggravated damage&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T13:08:53-07:00","id":97691,"title":"","content":"I don't think the big brain is part of the inteligence charms. im thinking in ways to expand the monsters of myth concept to include intelectual monsters, like the sphynx.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T08:35:16-07:00","id":98381,"title":"","content":"Hm... hey, we should give Changing and No Moon Castes some society building charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T08:39:24-07:00","id":98383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98381#post98381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... hey, we should give Changing and No Moon Castes some society building charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you like septs, moots, and rituals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T08:53:53-07:00","id":98391,"title":"","content":"Whether or not they are the <i>best</i> philosophers, I think a Lunar philosopher sounds like an awesome concept, especially if they are in all other ways a conventional Lunar: half-naked and feral, roaming the wilderness, eating wild honey, and encouraging his disciples to go back to the city and break things.<br /> <br /> Basically, because of this thread my PCs are going to have to contend with Lunar Zarathustra, of <i>Thus Spake</i> fame. Is he the best philosopher or simply a charismatic lunatic? Either way, he sure does know how to inspire an amoral terrorist cell of intellectual pseudo-barbarians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T09:01:56-07:00","id":98395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98391#post98391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not they are the <i>best</i> philosophers, I think a Lunar philosopher sounds like an awesome concept, especially if they are in all other ways a conventional Lunar: half-naked and feral, roaming the wilderness, eating wild honey, and encouraging his disciples to go back to the city and break things.<br /> <br /> Basically, because of this thread my PCs are going to have to contend with Lunar Zarathustra, of <i>Thus Spake</i> fame. Is he the best philosopher or simply a charismatic lunatic? Either way, he sure does know how to inspire an amoral terrorist cell of intellectual pseudo-barbarians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved it until the encouraging destruction part. DOn't get me wrong im not saying its not cool, jst that i'll like it more if its a more positive outlook at life.<br /> <br /> . Douglas adams wrote in one of the hitchhikers guides that humans thought they were the most intelligent race in the planet because they invented the wheel, and discovered fire and make war. Dolphins belived they were the most inteligent race on the planet precisely because they didn't invented any of those things.<br /> <br /> A lunar philosopher drawing from this idea, living happy and unbothered in the jungle eating wild honey sounds incredibly fun to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T09:29:33-07:00","id":98413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98395#post98395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loved it until the encouraging destruction part. DOn't get me wrong im not saying its not cool, jst that i'll like it more if its a more positive outlook at life.<br /> <br /> . Douglas adams wrote in one of the hitchhikers guides that humans thought they were the most intelligent race in the planet because they invented the wheel, and discovered fire and make war. Dolphins belived they were the most inteligent race on the planet precisely because they didn't invented any of those things.<br /> <br /> A lunar philosopher drawing from this idea, living happy and unbothered in the jungle eating wild honey sounds incredibly fun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm basing him off Nietzche's author-insert character in <i>Thus Spake Zarathustra,</i> who frequently denounces the society he has distanced himself from, commenting on how the population is too large, people suppress their Will to Power, etc. I figure this mind-set dovetails nicely with the 3E depictions of Lunars we've seen thus far as a constant barbaric menace to the Realm.<br /> <br /> It's also definitely intended as an NPC concept: he's going to do a lot of waxing philosophical and stroking his ragged beard while things burn, leaving the PCs to wonder if his violent agenda is really evidence of his enlightenment, or if he's just a murderer with a big vocabulary. He'll pop up periodically throughout the campaign, killing someone or breaking something that isn't theirs (and may even be their enemies, since I'm going to run a Solar game first), and I'll leave them to decide whether to oppose him on principle or not.<br /> <br /> You could <i>definitely</i> also run a much more carefree Lunar philosopher, a la Rafiki from the Lion King or Ba-loo the Bear from the Jungle Book, though. That'd be a great PC to play, I agree! It'd also help you cut down on the &quot;too many ambitions in the party&quot; problem, since he'd probably be content to ride along with his friends, help them out, and dispense sage wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T10:31:26-07:00","id":98462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98413#post98413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I'm basing him off Nietzche's author-insert character in <i>Thus Spake Zarathustra,</i> who frequently denounces the society he has distanced himself from, commenting on how the population is too large, people suppress their Will to Power, etc. I figure this mind-set dovetails nicely with the 3E depictions of Lunars we've seen thus far as a constant barbaric menace to the Realm.<br /> <br /> It's also definitely intended as an NPC concept: he's going to do a lot of waxing philosophical and stroking his ragged beard while things burn, leaving the PCs to wonder if his violent agenda is really evidence of his enlightenment, or if he's just a murderer with a big vocabulary. He'll pop up periodically throughout the campaign, killing someone or breaking something that isn't theirs (and may even be their enemies, since I'm going to run a Solar game first), and I'll leave them to decide whether to oppose him on principle or not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As an NPC it is interesting. Maybe contrast his actions by having him destroy clearly evil objectives but without discrimination for colateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T14:52:41-07:00","id":98682,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Greatest Philosopher in the World!&quot; is a Solar concept, because &quot;The Greatest [human achievement] in the World!&quot; is <i>always</i> a Solar concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T15:09:56-07:00","id":98699,"title":"","content":"Philosophy seems like a very Solar-y thing anyway, regardless of Solars being the chosen of the God of Arete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T15:25:05-07:00","id":98707,"title":"","content":"I think i agree with you now. Even if lunars are more inteligent (they intelligence charms technically improve their intelligence and not some atribute) their inteligence is not honed or focused by training and skill. maybe their philosohpers get stuck centuries with an argument without reaching a satisfactory conclusion or have great and sudden insight, but that doesn't makes them the best philosophers of creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:30:48-07:00","id":98758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97640#post97640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To comment on the actual question: No I do not think Lunars make philosophers for the same reason that no one else does, its too important to the setting that no one has a strong handle on it.<br /> <br /> As Holden has said, there is no magic to rule with grace and wisdom. There is no charm to make a perfect world even though there are charms to create worlds. The questions about what Creation should look like and what the place of anything in it should be are ones everyone has to try to answer for themselves. Just because the Solar's utopian vision would be very shiny does not make it a good thing or better then the Sidereal's safe, stable, and soul-crushing plan. They have to settle it with their fists or with their after effects, and everything will constantly be in motion as they attempt to deal with each other. No easy answers to be found.<br /> <br /> At best, charms should make you better at picking holes in other people's ideas by improving your ability to consider consequences and structural problems. Those same charms would also make you better at refuting the flaws you or others find and to prop up a bad system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with this, in a sense, &quot;The Greatest Philosopher in the World&quot; can't reeeeaaaly be a Solar concept. <br /> <br /> Because if philosophy to the moral domain, it does seem to essentially be &quot;I am the wisest&quot; and Solars don't get that. Wisdom, is formed strongly by intuition, character and experience, which aren't skills and aren't particularly nourished by the Solar Exaltation (they're part of what contributes to skills, but not actually a skill), or really any other Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Solars would get to be the philosophers who philosophize and argue with the clearest clarity and persuasiveness though, all things equal (which of course they never are, thus plausibly mortals who've had a particular insight, etc and thus end up being viable as &quot;the greatest philosopher&quot; etc like Isator suggests).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:48:47-07:00","id":98766,"title":"","content":"I think Lunar Ba-loo and Lunar Zarathustra should be BFFs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T21:42:23-07:00","id":98935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98682#post98682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Greatest Philosopher in the World!&quot; is a Solar concept, because &quot;The Greatest [human achievement] in the World!&quot; is <i>always</i> a Solar concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Greatest <i>at</i> Philosophy in the World&quot; sure, but 'philosopher' is a title, not so much a skill set, or a discreet function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T23:12:31-07:00","id":98974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98682#post98682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Greatest Philosopher in the World!&quot; is a Solar concept, because &quot;The Greatest [human achievement] in the World!&quot; is <i>always</i> a Solar concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>The strongest person in the world is not a Solar, the most charismatic person in the world is not a Solar, and the most intelligent person in the world is not a Solar. Because Strength, Charisma and Intelligence are attributes, not abilities. All of those people are probably Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure whether there's an ability that governs philosophising, but if I have a brain the size of a building, that should probably help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T23:29:47-07:00","id":98981,"title":"","content":"Philosophy is a Hell of a lot more than just brainpower or your mental baud rate. You can have a brain the size of a building, and have zero capacity to actually understand emotion, for example, which would lead to some interesting philosophical problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T23:46:14-07:00","id":98992,"title":"","content":"True. But with enough Intelligence dice, I can understand anything. And it is a point of fact that No Moon philosophers are more intelligent than Twilight philosophers.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, and in the absence of an ability governing philosophy... well... there's your answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T00:52:19-07:00","id":99012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98974#post98974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The strongest person in the world is not a Solar, the most charismatic person in the world is not a Solar, and the most intelligent person in the world is not a Solar. Because Strength, Charisma and Intelligence are attributes, not abilities. All of those people are probably Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure whether there's an ability that governs philosophising, but if I have a brain the size of a building, that should probably help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't we had this discussion before?<br /> <br /> There's more to being smart than the Intelligence stat on your sheet, and more to an Exalt's themes than what their prerequisites are. My opinion is that the broad thematic of being the most intelligent person around is simply more important to Twilights than to No Moons. (In fact, I might even argue that it's more important to Sidereals than to No Moons.) Historically, Twilights have always gotten many more charms that <i>express</i> aspects of intelligence, and I don't expect that to change in 3e. Lunar charm themes are also a bit vague in general, but I feel comfortable saying that expressing the legend of their abilities (including ones like Lore and Investigation, which imply intelligence) are more important to Solars than expressing abstract legends for Attributes is to Lunars.<br /> <br /> (Generally the Lunar charmset has gone to great pains to find other things to focus on, probably because the authors recognized that since almost everything is Ability + Attribute, and even the things that are just an Attribute often still fall under the thematic of an Ability, trying to structure Lunar thematics too heavily around straightforward applications of attributes dooms them to being Silver Solars. I mean, straightforwards applications of your attributes are <i>there</i>, but I don't feel they're a good thing to use as a central column of design for Lunars the way abilities are for Solars. Compounding this is the fact that attributes, unlike abilities, tend to be poorly-distributed in terms of what they do -- as we can see from Dexterity, for instance.)<br /> <br /> If you were to ask a typical historian in the Exalted Universe who the smartest or most charismatic person in history was, they'd name a DB (or even, possibly, a mortal) because everyone else has been erased from history or cast as monstrous outsiders. But if you asked some sort of Celestial Deity of History who had reasonably accurate knowledge going back to the First Age, they'd probably name a Solar, because the big memorable achievements that get you written down in the books as the &quot;smartest person in history&quot; or the &quot;most charismatic person who ever lived&quot; would generally be more likely to have been done by Solars.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be, like, 100% -- intelligence is not quantifiable and can refer to many different things, regardless of the fact that we have a stat for it out-of-character, and there are a lot of achievements by all sorts of different people. There would be other historians who might name a Lunar, Sidereal, or spirit as a dark-horse candidate for those positions, say -- but it'd be like people who say they think the Eagles are the greatest band of the 20th century. Anyone who says that is probably, for one reason or another, going out of their way to ignore more obvious candidates.<br /> <br /> (Also I do want to reiterate that Sidereals have a major claim on the general concepts of wisdom and intelligence themselves, since even with their ability to predict the future, an adviser needs to usually be able to at least make a credible claim at being one of the smartest people in the room. But in the ask-a-historian test I mentioned above they are disadvantaged because they've erased themselves from history so well that even our Celestial Deity of History probably won't know about some of their achievements; and even beyond that, an adviser or behind-the-scenes manipulator is less likely to get written down in the history books -- which probably suits Sidereals fine, generally.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-26-2014, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T01:03:26-07:00","id":99017,"title":"","content":"Sorry to disagree, but no, No Moons actually are more intelligent than Twilights and intelligence is indeed a stat on your sheet and it does mean what it says. It may suck that Twilights are generally less intelligent than No Moons, but they are. They start with less intelligence (assuming the same distribution of mental attributes) and they can't increase their intelligence at will the way Lunars can, any more than they can increase their stamina. I actually think this is an important thematic distinction between the two, the difference between raw, innate potential and mastery of skill.<br /> <br /> Aside from sheer intelligence, though, philosophy is largely about examining life from different perspectives. I don't really see anyone as being better than Lunars in that area. A Lunar philosopher has been the cat and the mouse and the bird and the cricket, and the greatest have been the ghost, the raksha, the elemental, the demon, the god. Combine that with the fact of being more intelligent, and I don't see a whole lot of room for doubt over who's going to have the better philosophical insights.<br /> <br /> I agree with you about Sidereals - I can easily see them competing for the title here, with their more esoteric wisdom and ability to perceive life's hidden patterns and truths, very different from the more intimate and personal wisdom of Lunars. But mechanically or thematically, I don't see the argument for Solars being Creation's greatest philosophers. Solars are the greatest of the Exalted and the greatest in many specific things, but philosophising doesn't seem to necessarily be one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-26-2014, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T03:32:30-07:00","id":99044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=97225#post97225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know of any splat that has charms that specifically enhance talking about metaphysics or morality. I hope no splat ever does get those, because a philosophy degree is basically useless and I can't imagine philosophy charms would be much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember World of Synnibarr (of all games!) had an attempt at making the skill useful; having a more flexible and open world-view gave you a bonus to resist insanity caused by Lovecraftian &quot;mankind is insignificant / the cosmos is without meaning!&quot; cosmic horror, and violations of the natural order.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T07:36:35-07:00","id":99155,"title":"","content":"As i stated earlier, im not arguing lunars are the best philosophers anymore, since i've been reminded that solars are the best at anything they set out to do. Instead i'm arguing lunars are the most intelligent characters and that gives them distinct advantages are certain endeavors like philosophy.<br /> <br /> First I'll say that agree that having that being smart is not the same as having most intelligence. However being intelligent is about having the most intelligence and intelligence directly correlates with the dots in the character sheet.<br /> <br /> And considering xp expenditure, its true that a Solar might have more specific charms for the endeavor, but they would have to buy at least Lore and Occult charms (and probaly investigation and some other charms too) to do so. While the lunar only needs to by his intelligence charms, maybe some percption charms, but that would mean the solar will need awarness charms too.<br /> <br /> Regarding recognition as measure of success as a philosopher, thats nonsense. Look at Aristotle, he was recogniced as one of the greatest philosophers of antiquity, and now almost eerything he said has been proven wrong, and some of his less recogniced contemporaries had better theories, mmore in line with the way th world works in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T07:49:50-07:00","id":99164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99017#post99017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to disagree, but no, No Moons actually are more intelligent than Twilights and intelligence is indeed a stat on your sheet and it does mean what it says. It may suck that Twilights are generally less intelligent than No Moons, but they are. They start with less intelligence (assuming the same distribution of mental attributes) and they can't increase their intelligence at will the way Lunars can, any more than they can increase their stamina. I actually think this is an important thematic distinction between the two, the difference between raw, innate potential and mastery of skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not an important distinction between them -- Solars actually get a charm to boost their strength, remember, because strength is also important to them. The only reason they lack one for intelligence is because they don't <i>need</i> it; intelligence (as a thematic and not a word on your stat sheet) is adequately covered by the charms they get in other areas. The definition of Solars is not &quot;skilled, but weak&quot;; their charms grant them the physical and mental backing necessary to show preeminence in the areas they cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aside from sheer intelligence, though, philosophy is largely about examining life from different perspectives. I don't really see anyone as being better than Lunars in that area. A Lunar philosopher has been the cat and the mouse and the bird and the cricket, and the greatest have been the ghost, the raksha, the elemental, the demon, the god. Combine that with the fact of being more intelligent, and I don't see a whole lot of room for doubt over who's going to have the better philosophical insights. </div> </div> </div>Philosophy itself is not a single unified thing, nor is there any strict measure of who is a &quot;better&quot; philosopher. But in terms of everything measurable about it, Solars are probably going to have the best charms. Who is going to write most of the setting's philosophical treatises? Solars. Who has the best charms for attracting adherents to their philosophies? Solars.<br /> <br /> Who is going to be able to produce a philosophy that will have the most beneficial impact on a society? To a great extent this isn't a thing -- the game doesn't give anyone an &quot;axiomatically make correct choices&quot; power. But to the extent that anyone has the ability to do it, it falls under Solar Socialize. Who's going to be able to learn the most about natural philosophy and the underlying truth of the universe? Again, not necessarily a thing in the larger sense, but to the extent that anyone does (and to the extent that people can show that understanding), it falls under Solar Occult, Solar Lore, and Solar Craft -- Solars will write better books on the underlying philosophy of the occult or the underlying philosophy of society or the underlying philosophy of anything they're good at, because they're good at those things. Additionally, philosophy beyond freshman navel-gazing requires knowledge of the great thinkers who come before, which falls under Linguistics and Lore.<br /> <br /> (Obviously, the actual 'best philosophers' remembered in the modern world are generally not Solars for the reason I alluded to above; in the modern world, DB and Sidereal philosophies win out because they murdered all the Solars and currently rule the world, and there's probably a lot of famous mortal ones, too. In most of the world, people don't read Anathema philosophy outside of, say, the Heptagram, which probably studies the philosophical treatises of First Age sorcerers in hopes that it helps them get better at Sorcery -- most of which will be written by Solars. But Solars have the best individual charms for doing the things I mentioned, in general.)<br /> <br /> What does Lunar Intelligence <i>do?</i> In general, it hasn't done much to help you with any of those things. Its thematic is more cunning trickery and strange magic. Excluding their excellencies, there is in fact only a single Lunar intelligence charm that directly has the thematic of &quot;think hard about new things&quot;, and it does so under the thematic of &quot;Lunar minds are strange and obsessive&quot;, not &quot;Lunars are just smarter.&quot; There are far more Lunar Intelligence charms for manipulating the wyld, for instance, or for producing unnatural wyld-themed effects, than there are for doing anything that expresses smartness.<br /> <br /> Philosophy isn't just &quot;make a philosophy roll to determine the effectiveness of your philosophy&quot;, that's dumb. To the extent that it's reflected in mechanics at all, it's the gestalt combination of your knowledge-gathering, knowledge-producing, and knowledge-expressing charms in the areas you want to focus on as a philosopher; and Solars, generally, have the best charms in all three categories in every field we'd consider a &quot;major&quot; realm of philosophy.<br /> <br /> How would you build a Lunar philosopher? Can you name the charms you'd take? I can name lots of charms for a Twilight, Zenith, or Eclipse philosopher-prince, with many obvious routes of expansion based on exactly what sort of philosopher I want to play.<br /> <br /> Now, that doesn't mean &quot;Lunars suck at philosophy, lolz.&quot; Lunars are doubtless good at writing about what I might call Lunar philosophies -- that is, philosophy approached from the unique perspective that their powers give them. You're totally right that shapeshifting does give them an insight into certain things, and they'd have a lot to tell you about that; they probably also have a lot of thoughts informed by their knowledge of the Wyld. But, you know -- while I still think it's silly to ask the question, and that, mostly, philosophy isn't a mechanical thing -- if you want to talk about which splat is more designed to support playing philosophers, in general? Or anything like that? Well, look, the knowledge you get from shapeshifting or the Wyld is excellent and all, but I don't think it can compare to insights on <i>socialize</i>, <i>occult</i>, or <i>lore</i>; and you're not going to be as good at expressing it to anyone else as a master of linguistics charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-26-2014, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T08:11:56-07:00","id":99175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99017#post99017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They start with less intelligence (assuming the same distribution of mental attributes) and they can't increase their intelligence at will the way Lunars can</div> </div> </div> </div>Any dice pool Solars have for an Ability they can use an Excellency for that uses Intelligence, they can increase by the value of their Intelligence, in addition to the relevant Ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T08:29:04-07:00","id":99181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=98974#post98974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The strongest person in the world is not a Solar, the most charismatic person in the world is not a Solar, and the most intelligent person in the world is not a Solar. Because Strength, Charisma and Intelligence are attributes, not abilities. All of those people are probably Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few ways to assess &quot;greatest in the world at something&quot;, and going by stats and dicepools in the abstract is probably the weakest of them.<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to view it through the lens of actual character deeds*, and to the extent that these are stated or implied, Solars are the ones who at least display deeds that carry the dramatic motif of being &quot;strongest/smartest/most charismatic in all Creation&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is not accounting for the level of subjectivity inherent to assessments of quality in the first place (secreted away in her private library, Jupiter possesses the only remaining copy of the diary of a mortal who spent five years making private observations about the world a few hundred years ago, and then suddenly died in a farming accident at the age of 22; she regards him as the greatest philosopher in the history of the world; she is neither right nor wrong in this assessment).<br /> <br /> * Well, actually, I'd be most inclined to view it as a boast, something that says more about the personality of whomever is making it (whether it be about themselves or somebody else) than about actual aptitude. This is not pejorative to me; there's definitely something fun to having a character declare themselves &quot;mightiest in all of Creation&quot;, but not to the point where the setting has to bend around supporting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T08:36:29-07:00","id":99189,"title":"","content":"In a followup to what I said above -- I think that if you followed the progress of philosophy from the dawn of the First Age to the fall of the Solars, what you'd probably see is several decent Lunar philosophers at the beginning, who eventually get increasingly overshadowed. This is not just because Solars grow faster; it's also because as time passes and more gets written, maintaining your credibility as a philosopher would require not just being able to publish yourself, but being able to keep up with the output of every other philosopher by rapidly reading and understanding what they've written. Without Linguistics and Lore charms, <i>even if we granted that Lunar intelligence gives you an edge in white-room thinking</i>, Solars will still win out because they'll be better at building on the ideas and thoughts from the past.<br /> <br /> (Lunars do have charms to preserve knowledge, mind, but not ones that are as useful in a wide-spread academic world. As a general rule the Lunar charmset is very good at operating in the wilderness with little support, but less good at taking advantage of established institutions -- which is a problem even for philosophers, since ultimately, contributing to philosophy in a developed society requires constantly working to keep up other people's thoughts.)<br /> <br /> But I do want to reiterate that this doesn't mean there are no Lunar philosophers, or even that Lunar philosophers are <i>bad</i>, by Exalted standards. I'm sure some of the books those scholars in the First Age read were written by Lunars, especially the ones from early on; and I'm sure that even the greatest Twilight scholars had something to learn by reading books by Lunars (and Sidereals and DBs and even mortals.) &quot;Lunar philosopher&quot; is a totally cool concept. But &quot;Solar philosopher-prince&quot; is also a totally cool concept, and IMHO it's more important to them (and more clearly visible in their charms, as a result).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T09:34:42-07:00","id":99233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99175#post99175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any dice pool Solars have for an Ability they can use an Excellency for that uses Intelligence, they can increase by the value of their Intelligence, in addition to the relevant Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it's not about how many dice you're adding to a roll, it's about how you're adding them. A Solar who uses the First Survival Excellency to add dice to an (Intelligence + Survival) roll to find food in the wild is doing it by improving his survival skills. A Lunar who enhances the same roll using the First Intelligence Excellency is doing it by <i>making herself more intelligent.</i> That's a major difference between the two Exalts, mechanically and thematically. One embodies attributes (potential), the other abilities (skill). Just as Luna and Sol embody those same things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99181#post99181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few ways to assess &quot;greatest in the world at something&quot;, and going by stats and dicepools in the abstract is probably the weakest of them.<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to view it through the lens of actual character deeds*, and to the extent that these are stated or implied, Solars are the ones who at least display deeds that carry the dramatic motif of being &quot;strongest/smartest/most charismatic in all Creation&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think their dramatic motif is more like &quot;the greatest fighter, the greatest socialite, the greatest scholar,&quot; strongest/smartest/most charismatic being measurements based on attributes, not abilities.<br /> <br /> I see this argument come up whenever someone suggests another Exalt is better than a Solar at something, because people feel it infringes on Solars' theme of unequalled greatness. But that's ignoring the mechanical basis of where Solar greatness comes from. Mechanically, a Twilight may be less intelligent than a No Moon, but she's still a better occultist and a better artificer. For the same reason that a Full Moon can be stronger, faster and more resilient than his Dawn mate, while still losing more of their sparring matches because the Dawn is the better fighter. Attributes (and attribute excellencies and attribute specialties) aren't the whole story. But they are pretty much the whole story insofar as innate characteristics like intelligence are concerned, and it is a fact in mechanical terms that when it comes to raw intelligence, Lunars have more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-26-2014, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:14:35-07:00","id":99267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99233#post99233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it's not about how many dice you're adding to a roll, it's about how you're adding them. A Solar who uses the First Survival Excellency to add dice to an (Intelligence + Survival) roll to find food in the wild is doing it by improving his survival skills. A Lunar who enhances the same roll using the First Intelligence Excellency is doing it by <i>making herself more intelligent.</i> That's a major difference between the two Exalts, mechanically and thematically. One embodies attributes (potential), the other abilities (skill). Just as Luna and Sol embody those same things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. &quot;Straightforward application of [attribute]&quot; is not as common as you'd think in some parts of the Lunar charmset -- <i>especially</i> not in Intelligence, where it is almost completely absent. This is because, again, while you can talk it up in the abstract, as a practical matter nearly everything in the game is Attribute + Ability, so defining Lunars as &quot;masters of Attributes&quot; would result in a charmset that is almost identical to the Solar one and themes that are almost identical to Solar themes, just slightly rearranged.<br /> <br /> Note that this is also a problem with the Lunar castes, which overlap with Solar ones very directly -- this is, I think, part of the reason it's been hinted that the old Lunar castes may not be coming back.<br /> <br /> Hence, Lunar Intelligence has few charms that embody the theme of &quot;smart&quot; the way Twilight charms tend to; instead, they're designed to go off in other directions, exploring the Wyld and strange interactions with the world. Lunars are still attribute-based, so it's not totally absent, sure, and there are a few exceptions; but in general (especially with the mental / social attributes) the thematic of Lunar magic involves things like strange trickery, animal themes, and shapeshifting, rather than just raw brute effectiveness with the attribute in question. If you want raw brute effectiveness in the &quot;I am unequivocally the best at broad straightforward thing X&quot; sense, you should play a Solar rather than a Lunar.<br /> <br /> The game already has a charmset that does basically everything thematically appropriate to straightforwardly being &quot;the smart guy&quot;, and does it as well as the game is likely to offer it; why do you want another charmset that is, at best, going to be a lamer copy-paste of that? It's much better for Lunar Intelligence to branch out into stranger Lunar-themed mysticism and leave the straightforward thinky powers to Twilights.<br /> <br /> (Obviously Lunars still get thinky powers, but I see them as being more like charms that let you think in a particular weird <i>way</i> rather than at particular tasks -- so you might have a charm that lets you make a plan to destroy something, or a charm that makes you better at planning complicated things, with broad applicability and flexibility rather than brute force.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-26-2014, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:19:07-07:00","id":99270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99164#post99164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not an important distinction between them -- Solars actually get a charm to boost their strength, remember, because strength is also important to them. The only reason they lack one for intelligence is because they don't <i>need</i> it; intelligence (as a thematic and not a word on your stat sheet) is adequately covered by the charms they get in other areas. The definition of Solars is not &quot;skilled, but weak&quot;; their charms grant them the physical and mental backing necessary to show preeminence in the areas they cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might have to fill me in here if I'm missing an important charm, but I don't think Solars have anything comparable to a Strength Excellency, or can use Strength specialties and whatnot, on top of having lower Strength to begin with. The Solar charmset is very diverse and powerful, but it all works off of abilities. I think that's for thematic reasons, because power in terms of attributes is seen as more of a Lunar thing. I didn't say Solars are weak - obviously, they're the greatest among the Exalted, but their greatness isn't expressed as raw attributes like strength, charisma and intelligence. At least not to the extent that Lunars' is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99164#post99164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Philosophy itself is not a single unified thing, nor is there any strict measure of who is a &quot;better&quot; philosopher. But in terms of everything measurable about it, Solars are probably going to have the best charms. Who is going to write most of the setting's philosophical treatises? Solars. Who has the best charms for attracting adherents to their philosophies? Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both true. The most eloquent writer (linguistics) and the greatest salesman (socialize?) are both Solars. I only give Lunars a theoretical edge in philosophy because it seems to be a consensus that developing philosophies isn't something that falls under abilities. But whatever rolls you would make to develop a philosophy in the game, I'm pretty sure having greater intelligence will make it easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99164#post99164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is going to be able to produce a philosophy that will have the most beneficial impact on a society? To a great extent this isn't a thing -- the game doesn't give anyone an &quot;axiomatically make correct choices&quot; power. But to the extent that anyone has the ability to do it, it falls under Solar Socialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you've lost me. What does Socialize have to do with making correct choices? To me, philosophy really seems like more of an (Intelligence + Highest Virtue) thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99164#post99164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does Lunar Intelligence <i>do?</i> In general, it hasn't done much to help you with any of those things. Its thematic is more cunning trickery and strange magic. Excluding their excellencies, there is in fact only a single Lunar intelligence charm that directly has the thematic of &quot;think hard about new things&quot;, and it does so under the thematic of &quot;Lunar minds are strange and obsessive&quot;, not &quot;Lunars are just smarter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Charm flavor text probably isn't the most reliable thing to go on. It's handier just to talk about what the charm actually does. Lunars, of course, don't have as many published charms as Solars because Solars are the default flavor of Exalt for the game. But they actually do have charms to enhance their intelligence, whereas I don't think Twilight charms are supposed to work that way. With Solars it's more like, &quot;You guide your mind unerringly to the right conclusion,&quot; rather than just, &quot;You quadruple your intelligence.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99164#post99164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you build a Lunar philosopher? Can you name the charms you'd take? I can name lots of charms for a Twilight, Zenith, or Eclipse philosopher-prince, with many obvious routes of expansion based on exactly what sort of philosopher I want to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting question. I think it would need custom charms either way, and/or an ST ruling on what, mechanically, is involved in creating a philosophy (if anything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:28:39-07:00","id":99277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99270#post99270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might have to fill me in here if I'm missing an important charm, but I don't think Solars have anything comparable to a Strength Excellency, or can use Strength specialties and whatnot, on top of having lower Strength to begin with. The Solar charmset is very diverse and powerful, but it all works off of abilities. I think that's for thematic reasons, because power in terms of attributes is seen as more of a Lunar thing. I didn't say Solars are weak - obviously, they're the greatest among the Exalted, but their greatness isn't expressed as raw attributes like strength, charisma and intelligence. At least not to the extent that Lunars' is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing Strength Exercise, in Athletics. Adds dots of Strength for the scene. It's like what Lunars would use a 5th Excellency for, if they had an actual one. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now you've lost me. What does Socialize have to do with making correct choices? To me, philosophy really seems like more of an (Intelligence + Highest Virtue) thing. </div> </div> </div>How are Virtues going to give you correct choices? They're poles of belief and passion. Furthermore, there is no objective right in Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Charm flavor text probably isn't the most reliable thing to go on. It's handier just to talk about what the charm actually does. Lunars, of course, don't have as many published charms as Solars because Solars are the default flavor of Exalt for the game. But they actually do have charms to enhance their intelligence, whereas I don't think Twilight charms are supposed to work that way. With Solars it's more like, &quot;You guide your mind unerringly to the right conclusion,&quot; rather than just, &quot;You quadruple your intelligence.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter. Lunar Intelligence is geared around being a cunning, long-remembering thing out in the woods. It's more about being like Mokole than an academic researcher, as the latter do not go into trances to sift through the dimension of memories for lost secrets.<br /> <br /> Also, much of what is published isn't a good bedrock because of the Silver Solar problem. Lunars in 1e had tremendous... issues in mechanical execution, among other problems. In 2e, this was addressed largely by making their Charms watered down versions of Solar Charms with certain restrictions in place, like &quot;no scene longs&quot;, which was really not a good idea, since Fury and such can't keep up, and Lunars don't thematically go along with the ideals of virtu and arete that the structure would suggest. They would have much more in common with the Alchemical Charms, all things considered, and even that would be a kludge that just shaves off certain capacities, such as being really good at industry, and adds others, such as shapeshifting expansion effects and having an easier time regenerating or growing claws.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:36:12-07:00","id":99289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99270#post99270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have to fill me in here if I'm missing an important charm, but I don't think Solars have anything comparable to a Strength Excellency, or can use Strength specialties and whatnot, on top of having lower Strength to begin with. The Solar charmset is very diverse and powerful, but it all works off of abilities. I think that's for thematic reasons, because power in terms of attributes is seen as more of a Lunar thing. I didn't say Solars are weak - obviously, they're the greatest among the Exalted, but their greatness isn't expressed as raw attributes like strength, charisma and intelligence. At least not to the extent that Lunars' is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing Strength Exercise, Essence 2, Athletics 3, Simple, Scenelong, no prereqs, capped at no more then Essence extra dots of strength.<br /> <br /> It is essentially the Fifth Strength Augmentation but better since there is no WP cost and you don't have to activate it more than once to get more than one dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:39:49-07:00","id":99294,"title":"","content":"I'll like to think that in general solars have the second exclence while lunars have the first. Solars are continously great at things they do and have have contantly great result. Lunars feats on the other hand are raw shows of atributes having a first excelencie means they sometimes have better results than solars, but most of the time are slightly below them or even worse than that.<br /> <br /> And i agree with tsk and everyone else who argues on favor of lunars being stronger, smarter or more charismatic than solars. I know that having atribute charms doesnt explicitly makes them have better atributes, after all the dicepools end being the same (atribute+ability) but it can easily be implied from the nature of their charms and favored attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:39:53-07:00","id":99295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99277#post99277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are Virtues going to give you correct choices? They're poles of belief and passion. Furthermore, there is no objective right in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real philosophies are often rooted in things like compassion and temperance. Yeah, lacking an objective &quot;good&quot;, I don't know how it would work in Exalted, but it seems like that's a decent place to start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99277#post99277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter. Lunar Intelligence is geared around being a cunning, long-remembering thing out in the woods. It's more about being like Mokole than an academic researcher, as the latter do not go into trances to sift through the dimension of memories for lost secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that Wits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:55:12-07:00","id":99310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99295#post99295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Real philosophies are often rooted in things like compassion and temperance. Yeah, lacking an objective &quot;good&quot;, I don't know how it would work in Exalted, but it seems like that's a decent place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're rooted in conceptions of them. Which feelings may or may not line up with. That's what makes them feelings and not ideals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't that Wits? </div> </div> </div>No. Lore-Speaking Method, a 1e Charm that allowed you to learn anything by meditating for at least half an hour, was in Intelligence. And while more than a few Attribute mins in 1e were screwy and made to fuck over the splat, that one made sense (minus being based on a Charisma Charm, anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:57:54-07:00","id":99312,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry to rain on everyone's parade, but the best philosophers in Creation are the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> 'Wait, Mercury!', I hear you cry, 'How can that be? They've got bad Excellencies, and a very limited charmset and they're neither as intelligent as Lunars nor as skillful as Solars!'<br /> <br /> That's all true, but what you're forgetting is the starting advantage. See, if you put a Lunar in a room and tell them to philosophize, they'll think long and hard before coming up with something simple and beautiful and raw, although they won't write it down so nobody will ever see it*. If you tell a Solar to philosophize, they will begin writing the <i>Grand Treatise of Virtuous Wisdom</i>, which will be very convincing but also suffer from the fatal flaw of being a book on virtue ethics.** If you tell a Terrestrial to philosophize... well, honestly we all know that Terrestrials don't count, so they'd probably produce some sort of Aristotelian nonsense and call it good.***<br /> <br /> If you tell the Sidereal to philosophize, she'll look at you all funny and then pull out her earmarked copy of <i>Everything The Maidens Say Is Objectively Correct</i> and ask what it is you want to know. You might think you can defeat this stratagem by asking things which aren't in the book, but Sidereals actually have charms to intuit what we'd think about something!<br /> <br /> Now, since our wisdom is objectively correct and other philosophies are not, it is superior to other philosophies. Ergo, the ability to intuit what we'd think about something makes one the supreme philosopher.<br /> <br /> Q.E.D.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Bam! Take that, prehistoric philoso<i>-phytes</i>!<br /> **Sick burn, virtue ethicists! I <u><i>got</i></u> you!<br /> **<b>*And</b> our Aristotelian contingent! Bam! I'm on fire!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:10:27-07:00","id":99319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99267#post99267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not true. &quot;Straightforward application of [attribute]&quot; is not as common as you'd think in some parts of the Lunar charmset -- <i>especially</i> not in Intelligence, where it is almost completely absent.</div> </div> </div> </div>How's it not true? Are you saying intelligence excellencies don't enhance your intelligence?<br /> <br /> And comparing charmsets is great, but it's not just about charms. A Lunar can start with higher intelligence than a Solar, and can increase her intelligence for less experience. She can also use Intelligence specialties and so forth, which the Solar can't. It's not just the fact that she has Intelligence excellencies to call on. Generally speaking, it's just a mechanical fact that a No Moon is going to be naturally more intelligent than a Twilight, all else being even.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99267#post99267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as a practical matter nearly everything in the game is Attribute + Ability, so defining Lunars as &quot;masters of Attributes&quot; would result in a charmset that is almost identical to the Solar one and themes that are almost identical to Solar themes, just slightly rearranged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if that's the only difference between them, which it isn't. All the same, though, attributes are a big part of Lunars, both mechanically and thematically, and the difference between attributes and abilities can't really help being part of the difference between Solar and Lunar Exalted, at least until 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:14:27-07:00","id":99326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99270#post99270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have to fill me in here if I'm missing an important charm, but I don't think Solars have anything comparable to a Strength Excellency, or can use Strength specialties and whatnot, on top of having lower Strength to begin with. The Solar charmset is very diverse and powerful, but it all works off of abilities. I think that's for thematic reasons, because power in terms of attributes is seen as more of a Lunar thing. I didn't say Solars are weak - obviously, they're the greatest among the Exalted, but their greatness isn't expressed as raw attributes like strength, charisma and intelligence. At least not to the extent that Lunars' is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength-Increasing Exercise, in Athletics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Both true. The most eloquent writer (linguistics) and the greatest salesman (socialize?) are both Solars. I only give Lunars a theoretical edge in philosophy because it seems to be a consensus that developing philosophies isn't something that falls under abilities. But whatever rolls you would make to develop a philosophy in the game, I'm pretty sure having greater intelligence will make it easier. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now you've lost me. What does Socialize have to do with making correct choices? To me, philosophy really seems like more of an (Intelligence + Highest Virtue) thing. </div> </div> </div>Philosophy isn't simply about making correct choices for yourself; it's about the correct choices <i>everyone</i> should make. If you want to play Confucius, for instance, you will need extremely high Socialize, and to the extent that charms can help, Socialize charms will probably be the most useful ones (possibly also Bureaucracy, although that feels like a bit of a cheat.) Linguistics is necessary to convey this philosophy to others so it will have a practical effect (which is more than just eloquence.)<br /> <br /> Of course, being the best philosopher in terms of being &quot;right&quot; in a cosmic or moral sense is not something the mechanics can govern; socialize doesn't make your choices cosmically 'correct', because nothing can do that. But it can help you ensure that they achieve specific broad purposes -- in terms of, for instance, producing a philosophy that reduces crime or corruption or causes other specific effects when implemented across a society? Solar Socialize is probably your go-to ability, and as a result, if you wanted to play Confucius, a Solar would probably fit best.<br /> <br /> (Or a Sidereal, but the focus would be a bit different.)<br /> <br /> Lunar Confucius... I mean, is it a cool concept? Sure, partially because offbeat concepts can be cool. But is it the first combination you think of when someone mentions Confucius, or an idea that naturally seems to come to mind when reading the Lunar charmset? No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Charm flavor text probably isn't the most reliable thing to go on. It's handier just to talk about what the charm actually does. Lunars, of course, don't have as many published charms as Solars because Solars are the default flavor of Exalt for the game. But they actually do have charms to enhance their intelligence, whereas I don't think Twilight charms are supposed to work that way. With Solars it's more like, &quot;You guide your mind unerringly to the right conclusion,&quot; rather than just, &quot;You quadruple your intelligence.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Charm flavor text is <i>absolutely</i> what you want to go on. The purpose of that charm text is to tell the story of each type of Exalted -- to tell you what they are. To me, both the text and mechanics of Solar charms says &quot;philosopher-prince&quot; more than any of the Lunar charms.<br /> <br /> In <i>general</i>, I would say that Lunars tend to have a bit more of a thematic of down-to-earth practicality to them; while individual Lunars and Solars differ, if I picture a Lunar-Solar mate pairing I have a much easier time picturing the Solar as a high-minded philosopher and the Lunar as a down-to-earth confidante rather than the other way around. This is a loose thing and doing it either way is obviously fine, but &quot;figure out the way everyone should live and convey it to them&quot; is more a Solar thing than a Lunar thing.<br /> <br /> (I'm deliberately ignoring the Thousand-Streams River here. Partially because we know it is going to be specifically excised in the new edition, and partially because it always had the problem that it was something the Lunars were defined as doing without being something that their intrinsic Exalted themes or charmset had any real support for.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's an interesting question. I think it would need custom charms either way, and/or an ST ruling on what, mechanically, is involved in creating a philosophy (if anything). </div> </div> </div>Yes, but my point is that I <i>don't</i> think I'd need any custom charms or ST rulings to play a Solar who comes across as a philosopher. I am very good at giving lessons (including spiritual or moral lessons) and producing texts to raise people's abilities and attributes -- I can convey intimacies, virtues, and heroic motivations related to my philosophy as good as or better than anyone else. Just with published Solar charms, I am very good at reforming organizations by implementing my principles, or getting an entire society to accept my ideas. These are, practically speaking, the only vectors where I feel the game is likely to provide much mechanical support for &quot;philosopher&quot; as a concept; and for Solars, these things are clearly the focus of entire charm trees, sometimes noticeable focuses for entire abilities.<br /> <br /> Solars also have a noticeable number of charms that express the idea of being focused on a high-minded concept; whereas Lunars tend to be more defined by personal relationships. For instance, Solars and Lunars both have Righteous Lion Defense, but the Solar one requires a commitment to an ideal, while the Lunar one requires a commitment to a person, place, or thing. Which one do you think better expresses the concept of a philosophically-minded character archetype? I can play a Solar with Righteous Lion Defense focused on pacifism or justice or some philosophical concept; you can't play a Lunar that way, because the &quot;default&quot; assumption about Lunars tends to be that they're more grounded and less focused on abstract philosophical ideals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-24-2015, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:35:55-07:00","id":99340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99312#post99312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Trademark intelligent delightfulness*</div> </div> </div> </div>Could one not then make the case that <i>the Maidens</i> are the best philosophers in Creation? Sidereals still have limits (however slight) on how often and easily they can intuit what you think about things, after all. Meanwhile, you either know or you ask across the Games table.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> In less creative flippancy, Lunars may not be the best philosophers in Creation, but their skillset contains the tool to <i>become</i> the best philosophers in Creation.<br /> <br /> <u>Pro:</u> This method can be achieved without any grasp of philosophy.<br /> <u>Con:</u> Some philosophers are known to be pretty dry, so a dash of salt is advised. Or earplugs, if you plan to bed them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 03-26-2014, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:38:55-07:00","id":99345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99326#post99326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Confucius... I mean, is it a cool concept? Sure, partially because offbeat concepts can be cool. But is it the first combination you think of when someone mentions Confucius, or an idea that naturally seems to come to mind when reading the Lunar charmset? No.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing you think of isn't necessarily going to be right. But no, when I think about Confucius, the first thing that pops into my mind isn't &quot;someone who's great at socializing.&quot; I wouldn't be surprised if Confucius was actually terrible at socializing - Confucianism advocates a rigid class system after all. I'm actually thinking more about, like, someone intelligent. And the Exalts who benefit from Intelligence charms are Lunars, not Solars.<br /> <br /> Again though, it's not just about charms. Comparing the published Solar and Lunar charmsets is never going to be entirely fair anyway because Solars, as the default Exalt, benefit from having a lot more published material for them. Those are not the only charms you can have, just the only ones given in the books. What's important is the underlying mechanics and themes about how the charms of each kind of Exalt are supposed to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99326#post99326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength-Increasing Exercise, in Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, conceded. Solars do have a charm that's kind of like a Strength excellency. I did not know that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99326#post99326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but my point is that I <i>don't</i> think I'd need any custom charms or ST rulings to play a Solar who comes across as a philosopher. I am very good at giving lessons (including spiritual or moral lessons) and producing texts to raise people's abilities and attributes -- I can convey intimacies, virtues, and heroic motivations related to my philosophy as good as or better than anyone else. I am very good at reforming organizations by implementing my principles, or getting an entire society to accept my ideas. These are, practically speaking, the only vectors where I feel the game is likely to provide much mechanical support for &quot;philosopher&quot; as a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you just want to come across as a philosopher, I don't think you'd need any charms at all. But that's kind of different from what you asked before. There are no clear rules for developing a philosophy ingame, so I said custom charms would probably be in order. If you'd asked what charms would be needed for any of the stuff you're talking about here, well that's different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-26-2014, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:41:34-07:00","id":99352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99319#post99319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How's it not true? Are you saying intelligence excellencies don't enhance your intelligence?<br /> <br /> And comparing charmsets is great, but it's not just about charms. A Lunar can start with higher intelligence than a Solar, and can increase her intelligence for less experience. She can also use Intelligence specialties and so forth, which the Solar can't. It's not just the fact that she has Intelligence excellencies to call on. Generally speaking, it's just a mechanical fact that a No Moon is going to be naturally more intelligent than a Twilight, all else being even.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that these intelligence+ability+Excellency rolls are going to have as their end result a number of successes. With their better dice caps Solars will general have more of those. Since in this context the result of the roll as measured by successes is going to be something like &quot;Useful philosophical insight&quot; the Solars will have better ones even if they are not as Intelligent in the raw sense because their skill and magic translates into results in the same way intelligence and magic translates into results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:42:52-07:00","id":99357,"title":"","content":"Do keep in mind, the preeminent philosophers in Creation at the moment are currently the Dragon-Blooded, who achieved that position by the time-honored technique of murdering all the other philosophers, then murdering everyone who refused to toe the line on the Dragon-Blooded philosophy. This should tell you something about how philosophical debate works in Creation.<br /> <br /> Also, belatedly: Lunars need a charm that lets you eat a book in order to internalize its contents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-26-2014, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:55:49-07:00","id":99367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99357#post99357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, belatedly: Lunars need a charm that lets you eat a book in order to internalize its contents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holistic Knowledge Transmission, Glories p.69.<br /> <br /> You don't <i>have</i> to eat it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:03:59-07:00","id":99487,"title":"","content":"I have to ask: How, exactly, are the Lunars starting with stats beyond what other Exalted can have?<br /> <br /> 5 is the cap on Attributes and Abilities before Essence 6, without Charms, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:49:43-07:00","id":99518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99487#post99487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to ask: How, exactly, are the Lunars starting with stats beyond what other Exalted can have?<br /> <br /> 5 is the cap on Attributes and Abilities before Essence 6, without Charms, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Lunars get more dots to allocate among attributes, and can increase attributes at a lower XP cost.</li> <li>They can start with attribute specialties, which effectively add dots, or learn them later with XP.</li> <li>They can enhance attributes directly using various charms, such as attribute excellencies.</li> <li>Charms like Impossible (Attribute) Improvement can be used to permanently add dots beyond normal limits.</li> <li>Shapeshifting.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":".  list-ed 03-26-2014, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:54:24-07:00","id":99523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99164#post99164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you build a Lunar philosopher? Can you name the charms you'd take? I can name lots of charms for a Twilight, Zenith, or Eclipse philosopher-prince, with many obvious routes of expansion based on exactly what sort of philosopher I want to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take lots of Dexterity, Strength and Wits charms and generally eat anyone who disagrees with my philosophy of &quot;I consume, therefore I am&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T15:20:30-07:00","id":99540,"title":"","content":"Lunars are very intelligent. They have enormously sharp wits. They are frighteningly perceptive.<br /> <br /> But what might help make them distinctive as great philosophers is their capacity for a broad wide experience.<br /> <br /> Lunars, fundamentally are shapeshifters. This gives them experience of people and different lives (they can drink and eat of others hearts, perspectives and memories), different ways of being a living being that could give them a wider and more general take on life and existence, and even being a human, than would be easy or possible for one of the other Celestials.<br /> <br /> For instance, a Lunar who could live as Tiresias did, in a sense, might have the advantage in thinking about how humans should relate to one another. It also might be an enormous advantage in terms of being able to persuade other people, who can know that you have been in their place.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine how it would be appropriate to express this in a Charm (or whether that's even necessary)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T17:24:21-07:00","id":99600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99523#post99523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd take lots of Dexterity, Strength and Wits charms and generally eat anyone who disagrees with my philosophy of &quot;I consume, therefore I am&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The official motto of the Silver Pact: <i>Sic gorgiamus allos subjectatos nunc.</i><br /> <br /> Not just pretty words...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T17:26:08-07:00","id":99601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99352#post99352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that these intelligence+ability+Excellency rolls are going to have as their end result a number of successes. With their better dice caps Solars will general have more of those. Since in this context the result of the roll as measured by successes is going to be something like &quot;Useful philosophical insight&quot; the Solars will have better ones even if they are not as Intelligent in the raw sense because their skill and magic translates into results in the same way intelligence and magic translates into results.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are charms to get around that, though. For instance, a Lunar with Inevitable Genius Insight (available at Essence 2) increases her dice cap to (Attribute + Essence), and also adds one success to all rolls regarding research.<br /> <br /> So for example, if a Twilight and a No Moon each had identical stats (Essence 4, Intelligence 5 and Lore 3) and were making an (Intelligence + Lore) roll to do metaphysical research, and each had 3 dots of applicable specialties (Lore specialty for the Solar, Intelligence specialty for the Lunar), and the Lunar was increasing her dice cap with the above charm...<br /> <br /> With those stats, the Twilight's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Lore + Lore Specialty), 11 dice. On top of that, he could add (Intelligence + Lore) from his Lore excellency, for a total of 19.<br /> <br /> The Lunar's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Intelligence Specialty + Lore), also 11 dice. She could add (Intelligence + Essence) from her Intelligence excellency, for a total of 20, plus one success.<br /> <br /> True that the Lunar is using an additional Charm, but it's one that can last as long as needed. And the example assumes that the Lunar has no attribute advantage, and that the Solar's Lore specialty applies, when realistically, ability specialties tend to be less applicable and Lunars tend to have more dots in attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-26-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T17:52:26-07:00","id":99617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99233#post99233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think their dramatic motif is more like &quot;the greatest fighter, the greatest socialite, the greatest scholar,&quot; strongest/smartest/most charismatic being measurements based on attributes, not abilities.<br /> <br /> I see this argument come up whenever someone suggests another Exalt is better than a Solar at something, because people feel it infringes on Solars' theme of unequalled greatness. But that's ignoring the mechanical basis of where Solar greatness comes from. Mechanically, a Twilight may be less intelligent than a No Moon, but she's still a better occultist and a better artificer. For the same reason that a Full Moon can be stronger, faster and more resilient than his Dawn mate, while still losing more of their sparring matches because the Dawn is the better fighter. Attributes (and attribute excellencies and attribute specialties) aren't the whole story. But they are pretty much the whole story insofar as innate characteristics like intelligence are concerned, and it is a fact in mechanical terms that when it comes to raw intelligence, Lunars have more of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all so much hair splitting, honing on in technicalities and vocabulary minutia, and for what?<br /> <br /> I can sympathize with the desire to frame Lunars in motifs of &quot;world's greatest X as approached from a different angle to Solars&quot; if only because their own motifs have traditionally been vague and underdeveloped, but the fact remains that, while the Solars are still core (and considering the mythology space they emulate), it's the kind of thing that will only ever make Lunars look like slightly less impressive Solars, and it's so unnecessary when they've got their own distinct myth space waiting in the wings for them.<br /> <br /> It's not about preserving the image of Solars, it's about rejecting an idea for Lunars that lacks credibility on several grounds, including that it's only relevant in the abstract.<br /> <br /> A person says &quot;Lunars can be more Intelligent than Solars&quot; than struggles desperately to find things in the system and setting that are relevant as functions of pure intellectual exercise. What's the point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T18:04:24-07:00","id":99622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99601#post99601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are charms to get around that, though. For instance, a Lunar with Inevitable Genius Insight (available at Essence 2) increases her dice cap to (Attribute + Essence), and also adds one success to all rolls regarding research.<br /> <br /> So for example, if a Twilight and a No Moon each had identical stats (Essence 4, Intelligence 5 and Lore 3) and were making an (Intelligence + Lore) roll to do metaphysical research, and each had 3 dots of applicable specialties (Lore specialty for the Solar, Intelligence specialty for the Lunar), and the Lunar was increasing her dice cap with the above charm...<br /> <br /> With those stats, the Twilight's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Lore + Lore Specialty), 11 dice. On top of that, he could add (Intelligence + Lore) from his Lore excellency, for a total of 19.<br /> <br /> The Lunar's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Intelligence Specialty + Lore), also 11 dice. She could add (Intelligence + Essence) from her Intelligence excellency, for a total of 20, plus one success.<br /> <br /> True that the Lunar is using an additional Charm, but it's one that can last as long as needed. And the example assumes that the Lunar has no attribute advantage, and that the Solar's Lore specialty applies, when realistically, ability specialties tend to be less applicable and Lunars tend to have more dots in attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, your argument is one extra Charm, and one success, at a hefty XP cost, makes the Lunar better than the Twilight in a corner case?<br /> <br /> Uhh, your argument is showing some pretty hefty holes here. You're using multiple Charms, and, frankly, a Twilight that isn't optimized vs a Lunar that *is*.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T18:17:13-07:00","id":99626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99601#post99601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are charms to get around that, though. For instance, a Lunar with Inevitable Genius Insight (available at Essence 2) increases her dice cap to (Attribute + Essence), and also adds one success to all rolls regarding research.<br /> <br /> So for example, if a Twilight and a No Moon each had identical stats (Essence 4, Intelligence 5 and Lore 3) and were making an (Intelligence + Lore) roll to do metaphysical research, and each had 3 dots of applicable specialties (Lore specialty for the Solar, Intelligence specialty for the Lunar), and the Lunar was increasing her dice cap with the above charm...<br /> <br /> With those stats, the Twilight's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Lore + Lore Specialty), 11 dice. On top of that, he could add (Intelligence + Lore) from his Lore excellency, for a total of 19.<br /> <br /> The Lunar's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Intelligence Specialty + Lore), also 11 dice. She could add (Intelligence + Essence) from her Intelligence excellency, for a total of 20, plus one success.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/BZyv3nt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:03:18-07:00","id":99642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99617#post99617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A person says &quot;Lunars can be more Intelligent than Solars&quot; than struggles desperately to find things in the system and setting that are relevant</div> </div> </div> </div>A person? Me, right? I'm the desperate person? Okay. Is there a reason you're making this personal now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99617#post99617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all so much hair splitting, honing on in technicalities and vocabulary minutia, and for what?</div> </div> </div> </div>What &quot;vocabulary minutiae&quot;? Seriously, I want you to say what about my comment constituted &quot;vocabulary minutiae&quot;, &quot;hair splitting&quot; or &quot;technicalities.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exthalion responded to my comment to say that Solars will have more successes in any Intelligence roll because of the lower Lunar dice cap. I replied to point out that, actually, Lunars can increase their dice cap for anything involving mental attributes, using a basic charm, from Essence 2 onward.<br /> <br /> What vocabulary did I even use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:09:40-07:00","id":99647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99601#post99601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are charms to get around that, though. For instance, a Lunar with Inevitable Genius Insight (available at Essence 2) increases her dice cap to (Attribute + Essence), and also adds one success to all rolls regarding research.<br /> <br /> So for example, if a Twilight and a No Moon each had identical stats (Essence 4, Intelligence 5 and Lore 3) and were making an (Intelligence + Lore) roll to do metaphysical research, and each had 3 dots of applicable specialties (Lore specialty for the Solar, Intelligence specialty for the Lunar), and the Lunar was increasing her dice cap with the above charm...<br /> <br /> With those stats, the Twilight's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Lore + Lore Specialty), 11 dice. On top of that, he could add (Intelligence + Lore) from his Lore excellency, for a total of 19.<br /> <br /> The Lunar's normal dice pool would be (Intelligence + Intelligence Specialty + Lore), also 11 dice. She could add (Intelligence + Essence) from her Intelligence excellency, for a total of 20, plus one success.<br /> <br /> True that the Lunar is using an additional Charm, but it's one that can last as long as needed. And the example assumes that the Lunar has no attribute advantage, and that the Solar's Lore specialty applies, when realistically, ability specialties tend to be less applicable and Lunars tend to have more dots in attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or... we could perhaps give them both Lore 5 since they apparently care about this, meaning the Twilight has 23 dice vs the Lunar's 21 + 1 success. Which averages to the same number of successes and still requires an extra charm for the Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99601#post99601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True that the Lunar is using an additional Charm, but it's one that can last as long as needed. And the example assumes that the Lunar has no attribute advantage, and that the Solar's Lore specialty applies, when realistically, ability specialties tend to be less applicable and Lunars tend to have more dots in attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two additional charms (attribute specialties require Flawless (Attribute) Focus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:22:40-07:00","id":99650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99647#post99647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or... we could perhaps give them both Lore 5 since they apparently care about this, meaning the Twilight has 23 dice vs the Lunar's 21 + 1 success. Which averages to the same number of successes and still requires an extra charm for the Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. So the Solar will not necessarily have more successes on that kind of roll. Without Charms, they'd have the same dice pool. With Charms, they'd be tied. Although the Lunar would be spending more motes, I think.<br /> <br /> The reason I used that example was just to show that the dice cap isn't necessarily going to be an issue in such a situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99647#post99647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two additional charms (attribute specialties require Flawless (Attribute) Focus)</div> </div> </div> </div>Intelligence excellencies are really something a No Moon should invest in anyway. Inevitable Genius Insight is a basic Essence 2 charm with no prerequisites other than excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:38:41-07:00","id":99659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99650#post99650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. So the Solar will not necessarily have more successes on that kind of roll. Without Charms, they'd have the same dice pool. With Charms, they'd be tied. Although the Lunar would be spending more motes, I think.<br /> <br /> The reason I used that example was just to show that the dice cap isn't necessarily going to be an issue in such a situation.<br /> <br /> Intelligence excellencies are really something a No Moon should invest in anyway. Inevitable Genius Insight is a basic Essence 2 charm with no prerequisites other than excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point stands, that a Lunar requires two charms to mitigate the dicecap advantage of a Solar. It is an unfair comparison to give the Lunar three charms to a Solar's one and say that the Solar does't have an advantage. With those same two charms the Solar could pick up something like Lore Essence Flow to raise their dicepool even higher or other charms to do things which are more interesting then adding dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:44:25-07:00","id":99665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99601#post99601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are charms to get around that, though. For instance, a Lunar with Inevitable Genius Insight...</div> </div> </div> </div>Inevitable Genius Insight and Flawless Attribute Focus are not exactly strongly within the bounds of Lunar thematics. The former is a gatekeeper Silver Solar Charm that tries to present, along with its siblings in RLF and ISS, the impression that Lunars have a &quot;real&quot; dice cap above their &quot;normal&quot; dice cap, but only through this specific Charm. The latter simply comes from out of nowhere, and has no real, intimate connection to anything involving being a monster. Much of MoEP: Lunars, unfortunately, plays host to Charms of these types, which give a very bad impression of what they're supposed to be like and what they're capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:22:12-07:00","id":99683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99659#post99659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point stands, that a Lunar requires two charms to mitigate the dicecap advantage of a Solar. It is an unfair comparison to give the Lunar three charms to a Solar's one and say that the Solar does't have an advantage. With those same two charms the Solar could pick up something like Lore Essence Flow to raise their dicepool even higher or other charms to do things which are more interesting then adding dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, but I'm not sure what your point is. We're not having a thread about who can buy the most dice with the least number of charm purchases, or at least I'm not. I replied to your comment about Lunar dice caps just to point out that it was actually possible for a Lunar to get the same number of dice on a hypothetical (Intelligence + Lore) roll as a Solar with equal ratings in those stats, because you had indicated they couldn't. I'm aware that you need the charm for it, as I said at the time. That's not news to me.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Solar could get Lore Essence Flow at Essence 3. Inevitable Genius Insight is Essence 2, not that it makes a great deal of difference. The relevance of the hypothetical (Intelligence + Lore) roll I used to the actual question of which kind of Exalt is better at philosophy (or more intelligent) is, at best, unclear to begin with.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how many successes a Solar gets on an (Intelligence + Lore) roll, his charms are still tied to Lore, not Intelligence. Intelligence is an attribute and is IMO more of a Lunar thing, mechanically and thematically, regardless of dice caps. Just like all the other attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99665#post99665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inevitable Genius Insight and Flawless Attribute Focus are not exactly strongly within the bounds of Lunar thematics. The former is a gatekeeper Silver Solar Charm that tries to present, along with its siblings in RLF and ISS, the impression that Lunars have a &quot;real&quot; dice cap above their &quot;normal&quot; dice cap, but only through this specific Charm. The latter simply comes from out of nowhere, and has no real, intimate connection to anything involving being a monster. Much of MoEP: Lunars, unfortunately, plays host to Charms of these types, which give a very bad impression of what they're supposed to be like and what they're capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying Attribute specialties aren't thematic for Lunars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-27-2014, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T21:11:16-07:00","id":99715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99683#post99683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, but I'm not sure what your point is. We're not having a thread about who can buy the most dice with the least number of charm purchases, or at least I'm not. I replied to your comment about Lunar dice caps just to point out that it was actually possible for a Lunar to get the same number of dice on a hypothetical (Intelligence + Lore) roll as a Solar with equal ratings in those stats, because you had indicated they couldn't. I'm aware that you need the charm for it, as I said at the time. That's not news to me.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Solar could get Lore Essence Flow at Essence 3. Inevitable Genius Insight is Essence 2, not that it makes a great deal of difference. The relevance of the hypothetical (Intelligence + Lore) roll I used to the actual question of which kind of Exalt is better at philosophy (or more intelligent) is, at best, unclear to begin with.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how many successes a Solar gets on an (Intelligence + Lore) roll, his charms are still tied to Lore, not Intelligence. Intelligence is an attribute and is IMO more of a Lunar thing, mechanically and thematically, regardless of dice caps. Just like all the other attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will be more clear:<br /> <br /> If Philosophy comes down to more then mechanics, then Lunar attribute advantages are meaningless. Actual wisdom and real ethical considerations are what matters and you cannot define what it means to be a good person even if you get a 1000 successes on an Int+Anything roll.<br /> <br /> If Philosophy does come down to mechanics then Lunar advantages in Intelligence do not matter in the qualitative way you seem to be implying. Other people, such as Solars and their better dice caps, have advantages of their own which are just as is not more effective in the task of throwing magic at the problem of accomplishing a mechanical effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T21:29:56-07:00","id":99727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99683#post99683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying Attribute specialties aren't thematic for Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very few things in the Lunar manual are thematic for Lunars, unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T22:41:21-07:00","id":99777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99715#post99715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will be more clear:<br /> <br /> If Philosophy comes down to more then mechanics, then Lunar attribute advantages are meaningless. Actual wisdom and real ethical considerations are what matters and you cannot define what it means to be a good person even if you get a 1000 successes on an Int+Anything roll.<br /> <br /> If Philosophy does come down to mechanics then Lunar advantages in Intelligence do not matter in the qualitative way you seem to be implying. Other people, such as Solars and their better dice caps, have advantages of their own which are just as is not more effective in the task of throwing magic at the problem of accomplishing a mechanical effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said this a couple of pages ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99270#post99270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only give Lunars a theoretical edge in philosophy because it seems to be a consensus that developing philosophies <u>isn't</u> something that falls under abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are only a few actions in Exalted that call for a roll of (Intelligence + Essence), or any other kind of roll in which an attribute is paired with something other than an ability. If it's anything like that, then of course Lunar Exalted would have to be the most proficient because they're the only ones who have the applicable charms for the task.<br /> <br /> If it's (Attribute + Ability), then Solars would likely have the advantage.with their ability charms. But it doesn't seem that it is.<br /> <br /> If it's not mechanical at all, then either Lunars or Sidereals can likely make the strongest thematic case, due to their keen intelligence and infinite perpective or their esoteric wisdom and ability to perceive hidden truths respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-27-2014, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T23:32:17-07:00","id":99787,"title":"","content":"I'm having a hard time seeing how, if it were mechanically represented, philosophy would be anything other than an Int + Lore roll or an Int + Occult roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T00:46:08-07:00","id":99812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99626#post99626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/BZyv3nt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey, Alcibiades, what does the scouter say about his philosophy level?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T00:58:14-07:00","id":99818,"title":"","content":"&quot;The scouter is just a shadow on the wall!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T01:30:30-07:00","id":99834,"title":"","content":"Int+Socialise, for political philosophy (as much of it is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T02:53:46-07:00","id":99862,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna point out that this is what treating Inteligence as objective measure of character's wisdom leads to.<br /> <br /> If we just accepted that actual inteligence is not something we can model with mechanics, this conversation wouldn't have turned into counting dice in Int+somethings pools and listing what charms Lunars and Solars have to make those pools bloated.<br /> <br /> Couple of pages back people were saying good things. Like that Lunars have more experience in seeing life from different perspective. And that Solars' story is supposed to be about being the wisest guy around.<br /> <br /> Those were some good points, why can't we have more of that, instead of counting dice pools that prove nothing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-27-2014, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T03:03:11-07:00","id":99867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99787#post99787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a hard time seeing how, if it were mechanically represented, philosophy would be anything other than an Int + Lore roll or an Int + Occult roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I myself wouldn't think this could amount to much more than a recollection of already absorbed details of an existing philosophy.<br /> <br /> The idea of rolling dice and then having the ST interpret the results as the development of your own life perspective seems eminently silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:12:55-07:00","id":99985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99867#post99867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I myself wouldn't think this could amount to much more than a recollection of already absorbed details of an existing philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as we all know, knowing the details of existing philosophy is never useful when developing some new philosophy, right?<br /> <br /> It's a perfectly fair point to make. Instead of just calling everything silly, how about providing some useful criticism?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99862#post99862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just gonna point out that this is what treating Inteligence as objective measure of character's wisdom leads to.<br /> <br /> If we just accepted that actual inteligence is not something we can model with mechanics, this conversation wouldn't have turned into counting dice in Int+somethings pools and listing what charms Lunars and Solars have to make those pools bloated.<br /> <br /> Couple of pages back people were saying good things. Like that Lunars have more experience in seeing life from different perspective. And that Solars' story is supposed to be about being the wisest guy around.<br /> <br /> Those were some good points, why can't we have more of that, instead of counting dice pools that prove nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's a fact that No Moons have better mental attributes; even if you eliminated intelligence, that would still be the case. It's hard to talk about things thematically without referring to what a particular kind of Exalt is actually better at than other kinds. But any discussion of Sidereals or Lunars being better than Solars at something is always going to be dragged into the same debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-27-2014, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T10:40:53-07:00","id":100156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99985#post99985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's a fact that No Moons have better mental attributes; even if you eliminated intelligence, that would still be the case. It's hard to talk about things thematically without referring to what a particular kind of Exalt is actually better at than other kinds. But any discussion of Sidereals or Lunars being better than Solars at something is always going to be dragged into the same debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okey, what do atributes have to do with philosophy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T11:28:12-07:00","id":100195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation#post97188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the fact that their splat is based around abilities, lunar should in theory be the best at abstract thinking. thing like philosohpy and riddles should be thing they excel at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll go you one better: Seeing as how Lunars naturally and easily raise their Attributes, that should mean that, in any gathering of Exalted, they are likely to be the best-looking, most charismatic, and wittiest conversationists there. Frankly, it's no wonder every Solar would want one on their arm! Maybe that's the real reason the Sids usurped them? &quot;Did you see how hot those Lunars are? And the ratio of them to us?? Man, if we pull this off, that's 3 Lunars for every one of us!&quot;<br /> <br /> More seriously, I know some people like to abstract the stats to just more dice to throw at a problem, but I still like them to actually MEAN something; otherwise, the core would bother describing what each dot in each Attribute makes you better at. So, yes, I would agree that Lunars would be the best natural thinkers among the Exalted, esp when you consider that they can even have Attribute Specialties (Int 5, Philosophy +3). <br /> <br /> Of course, once a Solar makes the effort to truly apply themselves, the cap on their Excellencies means that they can temporarily throw more dice at it, which must be acknowledged, so Solar Socrates can likely win a philosophical debate with Lunar Aristotle, which may lead some to argue that he cheated...which may well open up a philosophical question itself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T11:28:27-07:00","id":100196,"title":"","content":"Only that mental attributes help you think good, and thinking good is one thing that's definitely needed for good philosophy, whatever other requirements may or may not exist. Lunars can have higher mental attributes than any other Exalt, and are the only ones who can increase them with charms. Thematically, that's because attribtues represent potential (2e core), and Lunars are the flavor of Exalt whose gift is to embody limitless potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T11:34:39-07:00","id":100199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100196#post100196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only that mental attributes help you think good, and thinking good is one thing that's definitely needed for good philosophy, whatever other requirements may or may not exist. Lunars can have higher mental attributes than any other Exalt, and are the only ones who can increase them with charms. Thematically, that's because attribtues represent potential (2e core), and Lunars are the flavor of Exalt whose gift is to embody limitless potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;thinking good&quot; mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T11:37:38-07:00","id":100201,"title":"","content":"Self-explanatory, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:07:22-07:00","id":100224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100201#post100201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-explanatory, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Sorry, you gotta be clear, I'm a dumbass like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:18:03-07:00","id":100235,"title":"","content":"Think good is like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Uwbqr2UjeSg\" target=\"_blank\">jump good</a>, but with think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:47:05-07:00","id":100263,"title":"","content":"I'd say there's a fair chance that the &quot;best&quot; philosopher on Creation is a mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:54:59-07:00","id":100270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100263#post100263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say there's a fair chance that the &quot;best&quot; philosopher on Creation is a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>and why is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:04:18-07:00","id":100277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100224#post100224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Sorry, you gotta be clear, I'm a dumbass like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay then. It means being generally smarter.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to quote from the 2nd Edition core book, from the chapter on character creation, p.73-74:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">STEP TWO: ATTRIBUTES<br /> Once you\u2019ve defi ned your concept and selected your caste and Motivation, it\u2019s time to assign numbers to various traits. First, assign scores to each Attribute. The <u>Attributes define your character\u2019s innate capabilities</u> and aptitudes.<br /> [...]<br /> Physical Attributes define your character\u2019s <u>physical potential</u>\u2014how fast she runs, how much she can lift and how healthy she is.<br /> [...]<br /> Mental Attributes define your character\u2019s <u>intellectual capacity\u2014how quickly she thinks,</u> how keen her senses are and <u>how smart she is.</u></div> <br /> P.74:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">STEP THREE: ABILITIES<br /> Abilities describe what your character <u>knows</u> and can do, <u>what he\u2019s learned rather than his natural potential.</u></div> <br /> Mechanically as well as thematically, the main difference between Lunars and Solars is that Lunars\u2019 powers come from innate potential (represented mechanically as attributes), while Solars\u2019 come from learned skill (represented as abilities). It's the source of their beautifully dichotomous yet complementary natures. Like sun and moon.<br /> <br /> When a Solar enhances a roll of (Intelligence + Investigation) using one of his charms (like First Investigation Excellency), what he\u2019s doing is enhancing an ability, investigation. When a Lunar enhances the same roll with First Intelligence Excellency, she is enhancing her intelligence.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why Solars get more ability dots and can gain them more easily and have ability specialties, whereas Lunars get more attribute dots and can increase them more easily and have attribute specialties. Lunars are generally better than solars in terms of attributes - stronger, more charismatic, more intelligent. Because those are all measurements of innate potential. But Solars are supreme in the area of ability. They are better warriors, better diplomats, better scholars.<br /> <br /> (Attribute + Ability) is the key format for the game, and also the key to Solars\u2019 relationship with Lunars in 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:16:56-07:00","id":100285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100277#post100277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay then. It means being generally smarter.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to quote from the 2nd Edition core book, from the chapter on character creation, p.73-74:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">STEP TWO: ATTRIBUTES<br /> Once you\u2019ve defi ned your concept and selected your caste and Motivation, it\u2019s time to assign numbers to various traits. First, assign scores to each Attribute. The <u>Attributes define your character\u2019s innate capabilities</u> and aptitudes.<br /> [...]<br /> Physical Attributes define your character\u2019s <u>physical potential</u>\u2014how fast she runs, how much she can lift and how healthy she is.<br /> [...]<br /> Mental Attributes define your character\u2019s <u>intellectual capacity\u2014how quickly she thinks,</u> how keen her senses are and <u>how smart she is.</u></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok so, you're using Inteligence Atribute as a measure of how &quot;smart&quot; a person is and claim that the higher it is, the &quot;better&quot; you are at philosophy. I disagree. You'll have to convince me that being &quot;generally smarter&quot; (which I'm not sure I understand what it means) helps in philosophy, because I don't think it does. I'd even argue that the lower it is the better you are at philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:17:45-07:00","id":100286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100270#post100270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and why is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a definition of good philosophy as &quot;philosophy that is a functional and useful model of the world,&quot; then there's no action to &quot;do philosophy.&quot; You aren't gonna sit around rolling Intelligence + Lore until you come up with the categorical imperative or the \u00fcbermensch or process theology or whatever. It's subsumed into roleplaying. And, while the Exalted can be master savants and geniuses, genius isn't really a thing that maps directly into the realm of philosophy. There've probably been a bunch of Solar philosophers who've had very good ideas. There've probably been a bunch of Lunar philosophers who've had very good ideas. But there are way more mortals in Creation, and being mortal does not mean &quot;ha ha can never have good ideas fuckass.&quot; So while the orichalcum trophy for &quot;Best at Philosophy&quot; might go to a Solar savant or a Lunar mystic, it could also just go to an ordinary woman who has spent a lot of time thinking about things and had some very good ideas. <br /> <br /> (albeit devising the greatest philosophy ever conceived of in Creation is probably a good way to earn an Exaltation)<br /> <br /> That said, the mortal philosopher isn't going to be so supremely eloquent that her lectures make disciples of even the worst enemies, or so resolute that she can shake off mind-warping madness of the Wyld by asserting her philosophy, or so perceptive that she can intuitively sense when her teachings are being challenged within her philosopher-kingdom. Those deeds are the feats of the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:23:14-07:00","id":100288,"title":"","content":"See this? This one gets it.<br /> <br /> That said, you're ruining my fun mister Vance, please stop trying to educate people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:27:28-07:00","id":100291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100285#post100285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so, you're using Inteligence Atribute as a measure of how &quot;smart&quot; a person is and claim that the higher it is, the &quot;better&quot; you are at philosophy. I disagree. You'll have to convince me that being &quot;generally smarter&quot; (which I'm not sure I understand what it means) helps in philosophy, because I don't think it does. I'd even argue that the lower it is the better you are at philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that's not an argument I want to have at this point. But I'm curious - how does being less intelligent make someone better at philosophy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:38:51-07:00","id":100299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100286#post100286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are way more mortals in Creation, and being mortal does not mean &quot;ha ha can never have good ideas fuckass.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My base image of research work in Autochthonia is an Alchemical surrounded by a bunch of Sodalts as they all stare at the problem from the other side of an adamant pane, the Champion looking thoughtful with his hand on his chin while the Sodalts are oriented around him, coming up with ideas and discussing amongst themselves, while the Alchemical interjects with conclusions or questions that are guiding the whole process, but still kind of dependent on them. The range of perspectives and separate thought processes that are continuously playing into each other thus provides a more textured and efficient intellectual exercise. This image is more satisfying to me than an Alchemical who's just cloistered away coming up with all the brilliant conclusions on their own.<br /> <br /> It's an image I want to expand to Solars as well, in multiple fields.<br /> <br /> Certainly, while I imagine that Solar savants tended to be on the cutting edge and top of their fields in the First Age, and often with perspective and personal power capable of devising scientific and mystical hypotheses a mortal would be unlikely to, they'd still often be reliant on those ideas being transmitted out to the community of great research guilds across Creation in order to generate the necessary hard data, or have people who can see errors or propose addendum. It can come around from the other direction as well, with mortals who come up with their own new ideas that they lack the means to fully carry through, that eventually make their way up the chain until they get to an Exalt who can expand and clarify the edges of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:51:52-07:00","id":100309,"title":"","content":"I've said a couple of times in this thread that i think i was wrong. That lunars are necesarily the best philosophers in creation, mainly because being the best at they do is a solar thing.<br /> <br /> But i do think they are the smartest and by the same token, strongets and most beautiful of the exalted. Therefore, for me at least, the real question is wheter or not you think the lunars are smarter, stronger, more charismatic, etc. than the other splats.<br /> <br /> Regarding philosophy in particular, i think being smart lets you think out of the box and do some lateral thinking that allows you to overcome problems and resolve them in creative and diferent manners. The solar would study all philosophies in the world and use his lore, investigation and occult charms to interconnect what he has learn and reach a new conclusion. The lunar could listen to what the solar( or other philosopher or even himself) says and use his perception, witts and inteligence charms to listen to the meaning within the meaning and come to new conclusions based one raw intellect. In other words the lunar tackles a philosophy problem in the same way he works with architecture, engineering, or tactics, and its the best way to think, even though the final results might not be the best results.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:52:59-07:00","id":100314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100291#post100291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, that's not an argument I want to have at this point. But I'm curious - how does being less intelligent make someone better at philosophy?</div> </div> </div> </div>If by being good at philosophy we're assuming being able to come up with ideas then being less intelligent certainly helps. If you don't know a lot, you're free to come up with new things for yourself. You're not distracted by things you know. You're also more concerned with practical matters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:56:00-07:00","id":100316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100314#post100314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by being good at philosophy we're assuming being able to come up with ideas then being less intelligent certainly helps. If you don't know a lot, you're free to come up with new things for yourself. You're not distracted by things you know. You're also more concerned with practical matters!</div> </div> </div> </div>But knowledge is not inteligence, Knowledge is lore and occult and the other abiilities.<br /> <br /> And as other have said, one of the advantages of solars is that they have better abilities, they are better trained in the field and that helps contrast their thoughts with already existing theories and know were to loook for answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","user":"Quimeradc","date":". 03-27-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:04:08-07:00","id":100323,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Abiilities are what you know. Attributes are what you <u>are.</u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:04:44-07:00","id":100325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=99777#post99777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only a few actions in Exalted that call for a roll of (Intelligence + Essence), or any other kind of roll in which an attribute is paired with something other than an ability. If it's anything like that, then of course Lunar Exalted would have to be the most proficient because they're the only ones who have the applicable charms for the task.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic, it should go to high essence gods or demons? They ignore the human attribute and ability cap, have excellencies, and have their own unique perspective. If its a roll of any kind then Sol is the best philosopher in Creation and he produces the best results when in a philosophy contest with the god of philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:39:07-07:00","id":100353,"title":"","content":"Well, I would say yes, except gods have a lot of difficulty improving themselves, as I recall. They'd have to, like... get a promotion, or something, to actually become any smarter than they are.<br /> <br /> Plus, the philosophy of a god would be kind of inapplicable to humans.<br /> <br /> &quot;If a tree falls in a forest, a single mote will tell you whether it makes a sound.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;One candle can light a thousand flames, yet the sacrifice is not enhanced.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The wise man indulges not in eating or drinking when away from his sanctum and there is paperwork to finish.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-27-2014, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T22:27:58-07:00","id":101759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100299#post100299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My base image of research work in Autochthonia is an Alchemical surrounded by a bunch of Sodalts as they all stare at the problem from the other side of an adamant pane, the Champion looking thoughtful with his hand on his chin while the Sodalts are oriented around him, coming up with ideas and discussing amongst themselves, while the Alchemical interjects with conclusions or questions that are guiding the whole process, but still kind of dependent on them. The range of perspectives and separate thought processes that are continuously playing into each other thus provides a more textured and efficient intellectual exercise. This image is more satisfying to me than an Alchemical who's just cloistered away coming up with all the brilliant conclusions on their own.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically, they are the Dr. Houses of Autochthonia?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T22:45:37-07:00","id":101768,"title":"","content":"~<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100314#post100314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by being good at philosophy we're assuming being able to come up with ideas then being less intelligent certainly helps. If you don't know a lot, you're free to come up with new things for yourself. You're not distracted by things you know. You're also more concerned with practical matters!</div> </div> </div> </div> As mentioned, knowledge and intellect are different things. Frankly, I would say that creativity is different from intelligence, but for our purposes, they're grouped under the same Attribute, so we'll go with that. You could very easily have a character with a great deal of knowledge (high Lore/Occult), but low Int, meaning that he can recite a lot of facts and figures, but can't do much with them, creatively. Contrariwise, you could have another character with low Lore/Occult, and maybe even little Linguistics, to reflect illiteracy, but very high Int, and that would be your unschooled, natural philosopher who can come up with unique, original ideas that stymie the learned folk.<br /> Someone with low intelligence caught up in practical matters is more likely to just operate by rote, and not THINK about anything as he does so. It's the intelligence trait that lets him extrapolate a greater truth from the mundane world around him (remember the bath tub &quot;eureka!&quot; story)...<br /> So I don't see low int making one a better philosopher. If the argument is that there are more humans who are philosophers than Exalted simply because there are always more OF them, then yeah, sure. But I'm not sure how that equates to them being *better* at it...whatever that means (being able to come up with ideas, argue them or write papers about them? Exalted have charms and excellencies for all that).<br /> \u200b Then again, what IS philosophy, in the context of Creation, anyway?<br /> In RL, philosophy is a thing because, so far as we can tell, there is no actual objective truth to life and reality. Or if there is one, then it is hidden (or at least, not obvious) and must be puzzled out. Creation, as the name implies, is an (artifically? supernaturally?) constructed reality, and the nature and purpose of life and reality are quite literally a matter of record, that can be looked up in Heaven, as set by the creators of all. Given that, should &quot;philosophy&quot; as we know it, even be a thing? Or if it does exist, what form is it likely to take in Creation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T23:14:37-07:00","id":101779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101768#post101768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b Then again, what IS philosophy, in the context of Creation, anyway?<br /> In RL, philosophy is a thing because, so far as we can tell, there is no actual objective truth to life and reality. Or if there is one, then it is hidden (or at least, not obvious) and must be puzzled out. Creation, as the name implies, is an (artifically? supernaturally?) constructed reality, and the nature and purpose of life and reality are quite literally a matter of record, that can be looked up in Heaven, as set by the creators of all. Given that, should &quot;philosophy&quot; as we know it, even be a thing? Or if it does exist, what form is it likely to take in Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Philosophy encompasses numerous areas of thought and reality, and several of them are entirely unaffected by being considered from the eye of a transcendental myth-cauldron. Ethics for example appears to be alive and well given the numerous debates on the morality of the Titans/Gods/Sidereals/etc.. The stuff on record in Heaven, so called Natural Philosophy, would require the most significant overhaul, but could generally be practiced in much the same way. Its just that people would pointedly avoid complementing She Who Lives for this or that elegant feature of motonic interaction they just discovered instead of praising God for the beauty of mathematics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-30-2014, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T01:29:19-07:00","id":101816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=100195#post100195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, once a Solar makes the effort to truly apply themselves, the cap on their Excellencies means that they can temporarily throw more dice at it, which must be acknowledged, so Solar Socrates can likely win a philosophical debate with Lunar Aristotle, which may lead some to argue that he cheated...which may well open up a philosophical question itself!</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in Exalted 2nd edition, Lunars can get higher dice pools than Solars.<br /> <br /> A Lunar with Essence 5, Intelligence 6 (Thanks to the Impossible [Attribute] Improvement general charm) and 5 dice in Lore with a 3 dot specialty.<br /> <br /> This gives the Lunar a base pool of 14 dice. She can add an additional 6 dice thanks to the First Excellency for a total of 20. Then activating Inevitable Genius Insight allows her to increase the cap on Excellencies by her Essence (5) for a total of 25 dice; further Inevitable Genius Insight adds an automatic success, which is roughly equal in value to 2 rolled dice.<br /> <br /> So essentially the Lunar can potentially get an effective dice pool of 27 dice on a mental roll dealing with a very specific subject.<br /> <br /> Solars are usually sitting at a dice cap of 23 (5 stat, 5 Ability, 3 specialty + 10 dice from an Excellency).<br /> <br /> The discrepancy gets higher when you compare physical dice pools as Devastating Ogre Enhancement adds 2 to the Lunar's physical Attributes, potentially giving her say, 8 Dex, 5 Melee, 3 specialty for a total of 16 base, and with Relentless Lunar Fury allows her to add an addition (8 + 5) dice for a total of 29. And of course the automatic success from RLF essentially acts as 2 rolled dice, so effectively the Lunar is rolling a dicepool of 31 to a Solar's 23.<br /> <br /> On the downside, a Lunar can't sustain that high of a dicepool for very long at all; Instinctive Attribute Excellency only allows a Lunar to add 5 dice for free.So they;'ll burn out of Essence pretty quickly trying to keep those dice pools up for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-30-2014, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:36:13-07:00","id":101949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101816#post101816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, in Exalted 2nd edition, Lunars can get higher dice pools than Solars.<br /> <br /> A Lunar with Essence 5, Intelligence 6 (Thanks to the Impossible [Attribute] Improvement general charm) and 5 dice in Lore with a 3 dot specialty.<br /> <br /> This gives the Lunar a base pool of 14 dice. She can add an additional 6 dice thanks to the First Excellency for a total of 20. Then activating Inevitable Genius Insight allows her to increase the cap on Excellencies by her Essence (5) for a total of 25 dice; further Inevitable Genius Insight adds an automatic success, which is roughly equal in value to 2 rolled dice.<br /> <br /> So essentially the Lunar can potentially get an effective dice pool of 27 dice on a mental roll dealing with a very specific subject.<br /> <br /> Solars are usually sitting at a dice cap of 23 (5 stat, 5 Ability, 3 specialty + 10 dice from an Excellency).<br /> <br /> The discrepancy gets higher when you compare physical dice pools as Devastating Ogre Enhancement adds 2 to the Lunar's physical Attributes, potentially giving her say, 8 Dex, 5 Melee, 3 specialty for a total of 16 base, and with Relentless Lunar Fury allows her to add an addition (8 + 5) dice for a total of 29. And of course the automatic success from RLF essentially acts as 2 rolled dice, so effectively the Lunar is rolling a dicepool of 31 to a Solar's 23.<br /> <br /> On the downside, a Lunar can't sustain that high of a dicepool for very long at all; Instinctive Attribute Excellency only allows a Lunar to add 5 dice for free.So they;'ll burn out of Essence pretty quickly trying to keep those dice pools up for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried pointing this out already. It just makes you look desperate, apparently.<br /> <br /> I would add, though, that Impossible Attribute Improvement isn't limited to giving you Intelligence 6. You might just as easily say Intelligence 20 since there's no actual limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-30-2014, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:56:48-07:00","id":101957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101816#post101816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, in Exalted 2nd edition, Lunars can get higher dice pools than Solars.<br /> <br /> A Lunar with Essence 5, Intelligence 6 (Thanks to the Impossible [Attribute] Improvement general charm) and 5 dice in Lore with a 3 dot specialty.<br /> <br /> This gives the Lunar a base pool of 14 dice. She can add an additional 6 dice thanks to the First Excellency for a total of 20. Then activating Inevitable Genius Insight allows her to increase the cap on Excellencies by her Essence (5) for a total of 25 dice; further Inevitable Genius Insight adds an automatic success, which is roughly equal in value to 2 rolled dice.<br /> <br /> So essentially the Lunar can potentially get an effective dice pool of 27 dice on a mental roll dealing with a very specific subject.<br /> <br /> Solars are usually sitting at a dice cap of 23 (5 stat, 5 Ability, 3 specialty + 10 dice from an Excellency).<br /> <br /> The discrepancy gets higher when you compare physical dice pools as Devastating Ogre Enhancement adds 2 to the Lunar's physical Attributes, potentially giving her say, 8 Dex, 5 Melee, 3 specialty for a total of 16 base, and with Relentless Lunar Fury allows her to add an addition (8 + 5) dice for a total of 29. And of course the automatic success from RLF essentially acts as 2 rolled dice, so effectively the Lunar is rolling a dicepool of 31 to a Solar's 23.<br /> <br /> On the downside, a Lunar can't sustain that high of a dicepool for very long at all; Instinctive Attribute Excellency only allows a Lunar to add 5 dice for free.So they;'ll burn out of Essence pretty quickly trying to keep those dice pools up for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I count 4 charms in your build. Lets see what an E5, Spec 3 Solar could do.<br /> <br /> Glory to the Most High lets the Lawgiver raise their essence and all dependent traits, so the Sunking busts it out and suddenly has E6, Int 6, Lore 6.<br /> 6+6+3+12=27 dice. Throw in Lore Essence Flow and they add 2-6 dice to that from stunt and consequently increased dice dicecap. This still leaves the Solar with a free charm like Epic Zeal of (Relevant Virtue) which adds 5 successes or effectively 10 dice thus pushing the Solar's effective dice pool into the 40s. (Though stunt and virtue channel would raise the Lunar into the mid thirties to be fair)<br /> <br /> The question is not &quot;Can Lunar's get higher dicepools then Solars if they specialize and a Solar doesn't.&quot; It isn't even who can get the highest dicepools in general.<br /> <br /> As I understand it, TSk's current position is that assuming A: Philosophy is a (dice based) mechanical process and B: Philosophy does not consist of an Ability+Attribute roll but rather something exotic like Ability+Virtue then Lunars have an advantage because they are the only ones with a relevent excellency.<br /> <br /> If philosophy doesn't come down to dice its anyone's game and some mortal probably had a better insight about the good life or the meaning of beauty by sheer numbers<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101949#post101949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried pointing this out already. It just makes you look desperate, apparently.<br /> <br /> I would add, though, that Impossible Attribute Improvement isn't limited to giving you Intelligence 6. You might just as easily say Intelligence 20 since there's no actual limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not desperate, just unfair to the other side since you are giving the Lunar more charms and a more optimized build for the situation. The question isn't if a Lunar Philosopher is better then a Solar meathead at philosophy.<br /> <br /> Also, Impossible (Attribute) Improvement raises the maximum level by one, so you are capped at whatever your natural limit should be +1. You couldn't buy it up to 20 with just that charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-30-2014, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:07:16-07:00","id":101965,"title":"","content":"What about adding in the mental equiv to RLF (away from my books, now, don't recall the name), counting &quot;develop/argue for a philosophy&quot; as a project? That's an indefinite duration, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:10:29-07:00","id":101970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101957#post101957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not desperate, just unfair to the other side since you are giving the Lunar more charms and a more optimized build for the situation. The question isn't if a Lunar Philosopher is better then a Solar meathead at philosophy.<br /> <br /> Also, Impossible (Attribute) Improvement raises the maximum level by one, so you are capped at whatever your natural limit should be +1. You couldn't buy it up to 20 with just that charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes absolutely no sense to say that Lunars can raise their permanent Intelligence beyond the limits of possibility, but only as high as 6. It's not a stackable-keyworded charm, but it really should be. It's not as if they don't already have Intelligence specialties that increase it to 9 effectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101965#post101965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about adding in the mental equiv to RLF (away from my books, now, don't recall the name), counting &quot;develop/argue for a philosophy&quot; as a project? That's an indefinite duration, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean Inevitable Genius Insight, it lasts as long as a project, yes. In other words indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:15:34-07:00","id":101971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101779#post101779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Philosophy encompasses numerous areas of thought and reality, and several of them are entirely unaffected by being considered from the eye of a transcendental myth-cauldron. Ethics for example appears to be alive and well given the numerous debates on the morality of the Titans/Gods/Sidereals/etc.. The stuff on record in Heaven, so called Natural Philosophy, would require the most significant overhaul, but could generally be practiced in much the same way. Its just that people would pointedly avoid complementing She Who Lives for this or that elegant feature of motonic interaction they just discovered instead of praising God for the beauty of mathematics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points, esp interesting as how politics might influence the &quot;search for Truth&quot;. Still, given that the &quot;everything in Creation has a god&quot; also applies to ideas and concepts, philosophy should be no different. Creation is a world where it should totally be possible to climb a heavenly mountain and study under the God of philosophy's guidance. As to Ethics, considering that TUS pretty much invented that, I wouldn't be surprised if he or one of his entourage, such as the Golden Lord or Nysela, were considered to be that god.<br /> <br /> Not that you have to agree with him/them.<br /> <br /> In RL, if God turns out to truly exist, and shows up and says &quot;this is how things really are&quot;, then does that make eons of brilliant philosophizing suddenly wrong and pointless? Objectively, I suppose it would have to, but I can see many people refusing to accept that conclusion, even if they believe that God is who he says he is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:18:38-07:00","id":101973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101970#post101970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes absolutely no sense to say that Lunars can raise their permanent Intelligence beyond the limits of possibility, but only as high as 6. It's not a stackable-keyworded charm, but it really should be. It's not as if they don't already have Intelligence specialties that increase it to 9 effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making it Stackable would likely entail a number of counterbalances also taken from the Alchemical Charm set, with regard to the Fourth Attribute Augmentation. Though, really, a complete replacement of Lunar Charms blah blah blah damn I can't wait until the next edition delivers us from Silver Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you mean Inevitable Genius Insight, it lasts as long as a project, yes. In other words indefinitely. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6XyEZEXjq6U\" target=\"_blank\">Topical song title for gatekeeper Charms, go!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:34:54-07:00","id":101980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101973#post101973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making it Stackable would likely entail a number of counterbalances also taken from the Alchemical Charm set, with regard to the Fourth Attribute Augmentation. Though, really, a complete replacement of Lunar Charms blah blah blah damn I can't wait until the next edition delivers us from Silver Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Impossible Attribute Improvement requires Essence 5; by the time it'd take a Lunar to really exploit it, other game-breaking charms would be tearing the world apart anyway.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure if this is what you meant by it, but I really dislike that term, Silver Solar. The way it's used on forums, it seems to just be a way of saying no one should be able to do anything amazing because it infringes on Solar territory somehow. &quot;What? Higher dice pools?! Better attributes?! F'ing Silver Solars!&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is, both Solars and Lunars are Celestial Exalted. They actually have a lot of things in common in this setting, as do the sun and moon. So yes, there's going to be some overlap. Or there should be, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-30-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:50:39-07:00","id":101996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101980#post101980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Impossible Attribute Improvement requires Essence 5; by the time it'd take a Lunar to really exploit it, other game-breaking charms would be tearing the world apart anyway.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure if this is what you meant by it, but I really dislike that term, Silver Solar. The way it's used on forums, it seems to just be a way of saying no one should be able to do anything amazing because it infringes on Solar territory somehow. &quot;What? Higher dice pools?! Better attributes?! F'ing Silver Solars!&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is, both Solars and Lunars are Celestial Exalted. They actually have a lot of things in common in this setting, as do the sun and moon. So yes, there's going to be some overlap. Or there should be, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The term is actually a criticism of the mechanics Lunars have had which essentially tried to build them as attribute Solars instead of unique in themselves. It was a joke in poor taste that to make a Lunar charm you would find a Solar one, change the fluff to animals, make it cost more or do less, and stick it in an attribute that seemed appropriate. There are many mechanical overlaps where this is noticeable. Alchemicals were touted as one of the best designed charmsets in the line and the quality standard by which attribute splats should be measured. It is not used in the way you are taking it, <br /> <br /> The attitude you have noticed is based on the understanding of Tier in which all splats were graded on power level. Highest was the Solaroid Tier which included Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals. Next was Celestial with Lunars, Sidereals, and Alchemicals (They were a tad funny especially in Craft). Finally was the Terrestrial Teir, where things started to get muddy with things like Dragon Kings and Raksha. Mortals were at the bottom. The writers have said Tiers won't be a thing anymore.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:58:23-07:00","id":102000,"title":"","content":"According to the 2e core book and all subsequent books, attributes, in Exalted, represent potential. It makes perfect sense, mechanically and thematically, for Lunars as the embodiment of infinite potential to embody attributes the way Solars embody abilities. Abilities are about skill. They represent (again, 2e core book) what you <u>know.</u> Attributes represent what you <u>are</u> and <u>can be.</u> And what Lunars are and can be is, of course, without limit.<br /> <br /> It seems that a lot of players never really grasped that concept, and so any discussion about Lunars as what they are in the setting results in a lot of people calling them &quot;Silver Solars&quot; based on the assumption that Solars (using your &quot;power level&quot; example) are supposed to be inherently better at things, whatever things you're talking about. Which, of course, they are not, never have been, and (I hope) never will be. There are lots of things Solars aren't the best at, and a large part <i>happen</i> to be embodied by their metaphysical mates, the Lunar Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-30-2014, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:04:21-07:00","id":102005,"title":"","content":"Yes yes, all those people who complain about Lunar's blandness is just playing them wrong and are incapable of grasping the awesomeness that is Lunar's themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T11:54:28-07:00","id":102081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102000#post102000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the 2e core book and all subsequent books, attributes, in Exalted, represent potential. It makes perfect sense, mechanically and thematically, for Lunars as the embodiment of infinite potential to embody attributes the way Solars embody abilities. Abilities are about skill. They represent (again, 2e core book) what you <u>know.</u> Attributes represent what you <u>are</u> and <u>can be.</u> And what Lunars are and can be is, of course, without limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>General capability is a Solar thing. Lunars are monster saints. All of their Attribute-based Charms should be keyed around being monster saints. General high capability and effects provide nothing interesting on this front. This is why the second go at Lunars is cited as having failed, though nowhere near as badly as the first go at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems that a lot of players never really grasped that concept, and so any discussion about Lunars as what they are in the setting results in a lot of people calling them &quot;Silver Solars&quot; based on the assumption that Solars (using your &quot;power level&quot; example) are supposed to be inherently better at things, whatever things you're talking about. Which, of course, they are not, never have been, and (I hope) never will be. There are lots of things Solars aren't the best at, and a large part <i>happen</i> to be embodied by their metaphysical mates, the Lunar Exalted. </div> </div> </div>The position that you're championing is one that I formerly found myself in back when this material was new and shiny and everyone was just getting out of the first edition Lunar torture chamber. After a number of years of digging deeper into everything, however, all the flaws began to reveal themselves. The organization was ungainly, with pointless prerequisites, fillers and of course, not much in the way of shapeshifting. There was no celebration of the game that Lunars had been born of. The meaning of the Spirit Shape and Tell was still left unstated. And, of course, there was Relentless Lunar Fury, which you had to take in order to get your &quot;real&quot; dice pool. Which was also so brief in duration that it hobbled the capabilities of the Lunars beyond belief.<br /> <br /> We all perfectly well understand what the book was trying to accomplish. And most everyone now realizes that it was far from the best way to go about accomplishing the task of making Lunars fun. It was an exercise in tick counting and using a repainted God Hand to temporarily be important. It was the system shrugging its shoulders about other potential forms and just not caring about how fauna was statted out, even though turning into animals is a rather noticeable feature of being a Lunar. And it also chained the Lunars to the Wyld even more viciously than first edition did, since most of their interesting, non-copied Charms had the rider of &quot;must be used outside of where everything important and interesting is happening.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is why many people in this thread are rejecting most of the theses of your posts. They simply just don't work as a comparison between Solars and Lunars. Even if there are certain small numbers of Charms that can just be shifted around a bit, like Righteous Lion Defense and Ox-Body Technique, by no means does it make it okay to make all Charms according to this scheme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T12:14:35-07:00","id":102095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=101957#post101957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, TSk's current position is that assuming A: Philosophy is a (dice based) mechanical process and B: Philosophy does not consist of an Ability+Attribute roll but rather something exotic like Ability+Virtue then Lunars have an advantage because they are the only ones with a relevent excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're going.<br /> <br /> Philosophy could easily be an Ability + Virtue roll and simply not have an Attribute. MDV, for example, uses Willpower + Integrity. While Lunars do get some charms to mess with their MDV's, it's clear that, as that dice pool doesn't involve Attributes, they're not nearly as good at that as a Solar.<br /> <br /> There is no official &quot;Philosophy dice pool,&quot; so who knows whether Attribute or Ability based Exalted would be better at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T12:21:54-07:00","id":102100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102095#post102095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see where you're going.<br /> <br /> Philosophy could easily be an Ability + Virtue roll and simply not have an Attribute. MDV, for example, uses Willpower + Integrity. While Lunars do get some charms to mess with their MDV's, it's clear that, as that dice pool doesn't involve Attributes, they're not nearly as good at that as a Solar.<br /> <br /> There is no official &quot;Philosophy dice pool,&quot; so who knows whether Attribute or Ability based Exalted would be better at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, assuming there is a roll at all. The devs seem to be dropping hints that there isn't any roll that will spit out the categorical imperative or the pragmatic maxim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T12:45:32-07:00","id":102112,"title":"","content":"I wonder... Is there a dicepool for breathing action? And if so, can we try and determine which splat has the highest dicepool for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:02:34-07:00","id":102121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102112#post102112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder... Is there a dicepool for breathing action? And if so, can we try and determine which splat has the highest dicepool for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stamina + Resistance. (^VVVVVVV^)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Technically, just to get more operational time when holding your breath, but, you know...</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T14:21:32-07:00","id":102165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102081#post102081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General capability is a Solar thing. Lunars are monster saints. All of their Attribute-based Charms should be keyed around being monster saints. General high capability and effects provide nothing interesting on this front. This is why the second go at Lunars is cited as having failed, though nowhere near as badly as the first go at it.<br /> <br /> The position that you're championing is one that I formerly found myself in back when this material was new and shiny and everyone was just getting out of the first edition Lunar torture chamber. After a number of years of digging deeper into everything, however, all the flaws began to reveal themselves. The organization was ungainly, with pointless prerequisites, fillers and of course, not much in the way of shapeshifting. There was no celebration of the game that Lunars had been born of. The meaning of the Spirit Shape and Tell was still left unstated. And, of course, there was Relentless Lunar Fury, which you had to take in order to get your &quot;real&quot; dice pool. Which was also so brief in duration that it hobbled the capabilities of the Lunars beyond belief.<br /> <br /> We all perfectly well understand what the book was trying to accomplish. And most everyone now realizes that it was far from the best way to go about accomplishing the task of making Lunars fun. It was an exercise in tick counting and using a repainted God Hand to temporarily be important. It was the system shrugging its shoulders about other potential forms and just not caring about how fauna was statted out, even though turning into animals is a rather noticeable feature of being a Lunar. And it also chained the Lunars to the Wyld even more viciously than first edition did, since most of their interesting, non-copied Charms had the rider of &quot;must be used outside of where everything important and interesting is happening.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is why many people in this thread are rejecting most of the theses of your posts. They simply just don't work as a comparison between Solars and Lunars. Even if there are certain small numbers of Charms that can just be shifted around a bit, like Righteous Lion Defense and Ox-Body Technique, by no means does it make it okay to make all Charms according to this scheme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said Lunars weren't a mess. For instance, your point about spirit shapes and Tells - on the headcanon thread, I've said that when I'm running, they don't even have spirit shapes and their Tells are very different. I know the legitimate issues people have with the written material.<br /> <br /> All the same. if you're trying to say that's the case for everyone who throws words like &quot;Silver Solars&quot; around, forget it. A lot of them have never even played a Lunar character, and it shows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T14:49:37-07:00","id":102181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102081#post102081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General capability is a Solar thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds kind of like there's a disconnect here, like you're arguing about what it should be while I'm arguing about what it is. In regards to what it is, in 2nd Edition, attributes represent capability and potential, and Lunars are better at using them; and abilities represent applied knowledge and skill, and Solars are better at using those. A Lunar is generally stronger than a Solar, - he has more strength, and his charms are based on strength - even though the Solar can actually apply his strength to martial arts and get better results. All Solar charms are learned techniques for channeling essence. MOEP Lunars (which some people hate, but it's the most recent manual for Lunars we have) makes it a point to say that Lunar charms are <u>not</u> learned techniques. The Lunar <u>already has</u> those powers. When he 'gains' charms, he is merely using more of his innate power. I'm not applying any interpretation to this; that's just the way it is, in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102081#post102081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are monster saints. All of their Attribute-based Charms should be keyed around being monster saints. General high capability and effects provide nothing interesting on this front.</div> </div> </div> </div>By saying that, aren't you denying a whole lot of what the word <i>monster </i>means?<br /> <br /> <b>monstrous</b><br /> <i>unnatural in size<br /> outrageous, shocking; terrifying<br /> extraordinarily great; </i><i>huge in scope;</i><br /> <br /> Lunars have monstrous strength, monstrous charisma and monstrous intelligence. Their capacity for raw power in all of these areas is beyond any other Exalt. Again, that's not my interpretation; for better or worse, it's just what it is. Regardless of how many dots of Performance or Presence a Zenith Caste Solar will ever accrue, his raw Charisma will be engulfed by that of a typical (used loosely) Changing Moon. And likewise will the Twilight scholar's raw intelligence be dwarfed by the No Moon's, however superior the Twilight doubtlessly is in applying his intelligence and learning to a particular problem. That's just the nature of the two breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-30-2014, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T16:19:21-07:00","id":102232,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that you keep using those words capability and potential. The way you are using them doesn't make sense in this context. Saying Attributes are capacity or potential and then saying Lunars are best at them is implicitly saying Lunars are the best at everything. (Especially when you start throwing words like infinite) A Solar also has potential rooted in their abilities which does not derive from their attributes. A Str 1 Melee 5 Dawn will probably eat a Str 5 Melee 1 Lunar. The Lunar does not have a greater capacity then the Dawn even though the relevant attribute is higher.<br /> <br /> Silver Solars is not calling Lunars knockoff Solars who don't get to be interesting or have nice things. Its a critique at the execution of Lunar mechanics which were knockoff Solar mechanics which didn't allow them to be interesting or have nice things. It refers to the current state of the crunch and not to the thematic or narrative of the chosen of Luna. (The fluff wasn't exactly kind to Lunars either, what with making them sit on their hands for two thousand years with something like a quarter explicitly waiting for the Solars to come back and do things again.)<br /> <br /> Also, that &quot;every charm is a learned technique&quot; thing is on its way out with Third Edition and wasn't really a thing in 2E except in so far as people made it a thing. A Solar chef using &quot;Never Dull Knife Technique&quot; could just as easily have mastered the art of cutting so perfectly that their blade never becomes dull. (Not hitting bone, sawing through connective tissue, etc.) as be making their knife indestructible with magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T17:09:33-07:00","id":102257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102181#post102181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds kind of like there's a disconnect here, like you're arguing about what it should be while I'm arguing about what it is. In regards to what it is, in 2nd Edition, attributes represent capability and potential, and Lunars are better at using them; and abilities represent applied knowledge and skill, and Solars are better at using those. A Lunar is generally stronger than a Solar, - he has more strength, and his charms are based on strength - even though the Solar can actually apply his strength to martial arts and get better results. All Solar charms are learned techniques for channeling essence. MOEP Lunars (which some people hate, but it's the most recent manual for Lunars we have) makes it a point to say that Lunar charms are <u>not</u> learned techniques. The Lunar <u>already has</u> those powers. When he 'gains' charms, he is merely using more of his innate power. I'm not applying any interpretation to this; that's just the way it is, in 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars do utilize their potential... to be deadly and cunning werebeasts, only without most of the weaknesses of that type of monster. Just like Alchemicals utilize their potential to be state-sanctioned, artificially-created heroes. And Liminals, if rumors are to be believed, use their inborn strengths to be Clive Barker and Kentaro Miura-esque horrors crossed with Frankenstein's Monster. They don't just have potential, all of their magic is bent a certain way around potential and that is how they use it. Like how, in contrast with Solars, the Abyssals and Infernals of the new edition will be channeling their skills through the Deathlords and Yozis, respectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By saying that, aren't you denying a whole lot of what the word <i>monster </i>means?<br /> <br /> <b>monstrous</b><br /> <i>unnatural in size<br /> outrageous, shocking; terrifying<br /> extraordinarily great; </i><i>huge in scope;</i><br /> <br /> Lunars have monstrous strength, monstrous charisma and monstrous intelligence. Their capacity for raw power in all of these areas is beyond any other Exalt. Again, that's not my interpretation; for better or worse, it's just what it is. Regardless of how many dots of Performance or Presence a Zenith Caste Solar will ever accrue, his raw Charisma will be engulfed by that of a typical (used loosely) Changing Moon. And likewise will the Twilight scholar's raw intelligence be dwarfed by the No Moon's, however superior the Twilight doubtlessly is in applying his intelligence and learning to a particular problem. That's just the nature of the two breeds. </div> </div> </div>You're just using monstrous as a synonym for great potential. That doesn't really add anything to the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T18:03:26-07:00","id":102283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102181#post102181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars have monstrous strength, monstrous charisma and monstrous intelligence. Their capacity for raw power in all of these areas is beyond any other Exalt. Again, that's not my interpretation; for better or worse, it's just what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not what the developers have said it is, sooo {shrug}.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:37:59-07:00","id":102315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102257#post102257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're just using monstrous as a synonym for great potential. That doesn't really add anything to the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using <i>monstrous</i> to mean exactly what <i>monstrous</i> does mean. To say &quot;general high capability&quot; is not compatible with monsters is to pretty much ignore the nature of what monsters are.<br /> <br /> <b>monster</b><br /> <i>a thing of great and frightening power, force<br /> a powerful person or thing that cannot be controlled</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102283#post102283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not what the developers have said it is, sooo {shrug}.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seriously ever played a Lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:55:18-07:00","id":102328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102232#post102232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that you keep using those words capability and potential. The way you are using them doesn't make sense in this context. Saying Attributes are capacity or potential and then saying Lunars are best at them <u>is implicitly saying Lunars are the best at everything.</u> (Especially when you start throwing words like infinite)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because there's a difference between <i>potential</i> and <i>application.</i> This isn't my own idea; it's how 2nd Edition explicitly defines these concepts:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">STEP TWO: ATTRIBUTES<br /> Once you\u2019ve defined your concept and selected your caste and Motivation, it\u2019s time to assign numbers to various traits. First, assign scores to each Attribute. The <u>Attributes define your character\u2019s innate capabilities</u> and aptitudes.<br /> [...]<br /> Physical Attributes define your character\u2019s <b><u>physical potential</u></b>\u2014how fast she runs, how much she can lift and how healthy she is.<br /> [...]<br /> Mental Attributes define your character\u2019s <u>intellectual capacity\u2014how quickly she thinks,</u> how keen her senses are and <u>how smart she is.</u><br /> <br /> STEP THREE: ABILITIES<br /> Abilities describe what your character knows and can do, <u>what he\u2019s learned <b>rather than his natural potential.</b></u></div>I'm using the word because I'm trying to stick to the vocabulary of the system. To say Lunars embody potential isn't saying they're the best at everything, because Solars by their nature embody peerless application of power and skill. If Solars' potential isn't technically as great as Lunars', it's at least immense; and in their application, they achieve things impossible for Lunars or anyone else to achieve. What Lunars are &quot;best&quot; at is simply raw innate power, possessing monstrous levels of intelligence, charisma, strength, etc. to draw upon. Thematically, that's because because those traits are all related to your innate characteristics, the things that define not what you've learned or can do, but <u>what you are</u> - and no one is better at defining what they are than Lunars, because that's basically the whole point of Lunars, isn't it? Lunars don't have the peerless excellence of Solars, but what they do have is an infinite capacity to redefine themselves. In that sense, they're about potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-30-2014, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T20:27:52-07:00","id":102345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102315#post102315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm using <i>monstrous</i> to mean exactly what <i>monstrous</i> does mean. To say &quot;general high capability&quot; is not compatible with monsters is to pretty much ignore the nature of what monsters are.<br /> <br /> <b>monster</b><br /> <i>a thing of great and frightening power, force<br /> a powerful person or thing that cannot be controlled</i></div> </div> </div> </div>We've already established that the use of &quot;monster&quot; here means a frightening, inhuman creature here when I cited werewolves and company. Werewolf, the cWoD game that the splat was derived from, just as Solars were derived from Hunter: the Reckoning. The game where you were a furious engine of feral destruction and by default possessed super-speed because of your anger (and/or might, depending on Fera type). This type of monster is what people mean when they say &quot;Lunars are monsters&quot;, and dictionary-based hair-splitting is not going to make a mark on that front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T20:30:58-07:00","id":102346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102345#post102345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've already established that the use of &quot;monster&quot; here means a frightening, inhuman creature here when I cited werewolves and company. Werewolf, the cWoD game that the splat was derived from, just as Solars were derived from Hunter: the Reckoning. The game where you were a furious engine of feral destruction and by default possessed super-speed because of your anger (and/or might, depending on Fera type). This type of monster is what people mean when they say &quot;Lunars are monsters&quot;, and dictionary-based hair-splitting is not going to make a mark on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're focusing on &quot;frightening&quot; and &quot;inhuman&quot; and ignoring &quot;powerful&quot;. Earlier, you said &quot;General high capability and effects&quot; are not what monsters are about. High capability is actually a great deal of what monsters are about. A monstrous thing is not merely and not necessarily frightening or inhuman; often it's just something incredibly powerful. And it can that in other ways besides simply being physically strong. Terms like <i>monstrous intelligence</i> and <i>monstrous charisma</i> are not dictionary-based hair-splitting - they're perfectly valid themes for Lunars, ones I've played quite often, and a description of a mechanical fact about Lunars in 2nd edition, which is simply that they have greater intelligence and greater charisma than any other Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-30-2014, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T21:24:01-07:00","id":102366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102346#post102346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're focusing on &quot;frightening&quot; and &quot;inhuman&quot; and ignoring &quot;powerful&quot;. Earlier, you said &quot;General high capability and effects&quot; are not what monsters are about. High capability is actually a great deal of what monsters are about. A monstrous thing is not merely and not necessarily frightening or inhuman; often it's just something incredibly powerful. And it can that in other ways besides simply being physically strong. Terms like <i>monstrous intelligence</i> and <i>monstrous charisma</i> are not dictionary-based hair-splitting - they're perfectly valid themes for Lunars, ones I've played quite often, and a description of a mechanical fact about Lunars in 2nd edition, which is simply that they have greater intelligence and greater charisma than any other Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm ignoring &quot;powerful&quot; because it's implied in being a type of Exalted. Emphasizing it more is what Solars do. Emphasizing weird, non-standard ways of working is the territory that everyone else exists in. Consider the difference between Solars and Sidereals for a moment - the former are very straightforward, while the latter derive their mastery of skills through the lens of esoteric mystical secrets embedded into Creation, and while certainly not lacking for potency, Sidereal Martial Arts don't tend to emphasize 100+ dice of damage punches and massive knockback like Solars do.<br /> <br /> In essence, the only thing this &quot;greater (Attribute)&quot; affords them that can be compared to other Exalted is more dice, maybe. And, as written, they don't really match the Alchemicals on that front, either. Often, they don't even manage to get more dice than Dragon-Blooded with Ability 5 + Specialty 3. Very little in the system comes from having high Attributes - base time for holding breathing, movement speed, damage. That's the size of it. This is the &quot;great Lunar advantage&quot;. Once you start comparing dice pools, the origin of the dice stop mattering quite so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T21:37:06-07:00","id":102379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102366#post102366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In essence, the only thing this &quot;greater (Attribute)&quot; affords them that can be compared to other Exalted is more dice, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, greater Intelligence means you're <b>more intelligent.</b> Again, from the 2e core book:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Mental Attributes define your character\u2019s intellectual capacity\u2014how quickly she thinks, how keen her senses are and <u><b>how smart she is.</b></u></div>I know some players prefer to just define every statistic about their character as &quot;lets me roll dice&quot; but if you look in the core rulebook, you will discover that the intelligence trait, as well as the other attributes, actually does mean something. It means <b>how smart you are.</b> And Lunars have greater intelligence, greater wits, greater perception, greater charisma, greater strength, etc., than any other Exalt.<br /> <br /> Not only do they have more of intelligence, etc.,, they are the only Exalts who can actually increase their intelligence with charms (aside from some rare cases). They're the only ones with intelligence excellencies and intelligence specialties. They are more intelligent. All this nonsense about &quot;it doesn't actually mean they're more intelligent&quot; just strikes me as the royal butthurt of the sun-kings. Yes, it <i>does</i> mean that. That's <i>exactly</i> what it means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T22:19:23-07:00","id":102395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102379#post102379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, greater Intelligence means you're <b>more intelligent.</b> Again, from the 2e core book:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Mental Attributes define your character\u2019s intellectual capacity\u2014how quickly she thinks, how keen her senses are and <u><b>how smart she is.</b></u></div>I know some players prefer to just define every statistic about their character as &quot;lets me roll dice&quot; but if you look in the core rulebook, you will discover that the intelligence trait, as well as the other attributes, actually does mean something. It means <b>how smart you are.</b> And Lunars have greater intelligence, greater wits, greater perception, greater charisma, greater strength, etc., than any other Exalt.<br /> <br /> Not only do they have more of intelligence, etc.,, they are the only Exalts who can actually increase their intelligence with charms (aside from some rare cases). They're the only ones with intelligence excellencies and intelligence specialties. They are more intelligent. All this nonsense about &quot;it doesn't actually mean they're more intelligent&quot; just strikes me as the royal butthurt of the sun-kings. Yes, it <i>does</i> mean that. That's <i>exactly</i> what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoopty-doo. You can get to double your Intelligence. Solars can, too. Then they get to double their Ability. That's exactly what the dice mean. And with Infinite Ability Mastery, they get to keep on doing it, to an extent that Lunars, by RAW, cannot match. Intelligence alone only gets you so far.<br /> <br /> Stop banging the drum and drinking the Kool-Aid. There isn't a hidden advantage to be gleaned here, except perhaps to be better at a wide variety of things instead of just one. That's the special thing about Attributes, and it isn't exactly overwhelming if its big advantage is to give you half the number of dice on average.<br /> <br /> Also, point of order: Alchemicals with Essence 5 can get an Attribute up to 8. Not specialized. The entire Attribute. Any Attribute, including Intelligence. This, itself, isn't really so much of an overwhelming advantage, either, compared to Infinite Ability Mastery, the thing that's so broken it's going to be Charm Not Appearing In This Edition for EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:15:21-07:00","id":102429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102395#post102395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoopty-doo. You can get to double your Intelligence. Solars can, too. Then they get to double their Ability. That's exactly what the dice mean. And with Infinite Ability Mastery, they get to keep on doing it, to an extent that Lunars, by RAW, cannot match. Intelligence alone only gets you so far.<br /> <br /> Stop banging the drum and drinking the Kool-Aid. There isn't a hidden advantage to be gleaned here, except perhaps to be better at a wide variety of things instead of just one. That's the special thing about Attributes, and it isn't exactly overwhelming if its big advantage is to give you half the number of dice on average.<br /> <br /> Also, point of order: Alchemicals with Essence 5 can get an Attribute up to 8. Not specialized. The entire Attribute. Any Attribute, including Intelligence. This, itself, isn't really so much of an overwhelming advantage, either, compared to Infinite Ability Mastery, the thing that's so broken it's going to be Charm Not Appearing In This Edition for EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your only argument is going to be &quot;more dice&quot; or &quot;Solars have a broken charm that blows this up&quot;, then a simple solution is to ignore the existing rules for Lunar dice caps or houserule your own Charm or two. Nothing I'm even talking about has anything to do with dice caps. I'm simply talking about the basic mechanics, themes and vocabulary of the system. Intelligence means what it says, intelligence, and Lunars are more intelligent, stronger, more charismatic etc. than Solars. Whether that gives them more dice or they get more successes on a given roll is a completely different issue. Again, there's a big difference between potential and application. Even infinite potential is nothing by itself.<br /> <br /> And Alchemicals at that level - okay? So a freshly tattooed Lunar with Intelligence 5 (+3 practically everything) straight out of chargen is <i>only</i> as intelligent as a high-essence Alchemical who's had intelligence-boosting charms physically installed and... umm... uh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-31-2014, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:36:16-07:00","id":102443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102315#post102315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm using <i>monstrous</i> to mean exactly what <i>monstrous</i> does mean. To say &quot;general high capability&quot; is not compatible with monsters is to pretty much ignore the nature of what monsters are.<br /> <br /> <b>monster</b><br /> <i>a thing of great and frightening power, force<br /> a powerful person or thing that cannot be controlled</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I reject your definition of monster as useless. A monster doesn't have to be objectively strong, it only needs to be stronger than you for you to think of it as monster. To suggest that there are no things Lunars would consider monstrous is just silly. It's Exalted, there is always a bigger fish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-31-2014, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:11:14-07:00","id":102678,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so you find it and eat its heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:19:11-07:00","id":102688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102429#post102429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your only argument is going to be &quot;more dice&quot; or &quot;Solars have a broken charm that blows this up&quot;, then a simple solution is to ignore the existing rules for Lunar dice caps or houserule your own Charm or two. Nothing I'm even talking about has anything to do with dice caps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. Dice caps are based on something. If we're ignoring the origin of dice cap, your assumptions get knocked off at the knees... or would, if they could stand. Solars draw off of their capability and skill, not just the latter. That's what their dice cap of Attribute + Ability means. Lunars don't draw off their skill. That's what their dice cap means. This is not a matter up for discussion, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm simply talking about the basic mechanics, themes and vocabulary of the system. Intelligence means what it says, intelligence, and Lunars are more intelligent, stronger, more charismatic etc. than Solars. Whether that gives them more dice or they get more successes on a given roll is a completely different issue. Again, there's a big difference between potential and application. Even infinite potential is nothing by itself. </div> </div> </div>And Solars get both avenues. I doubt that Increasing Strength Exercise is the only Charm of its kind. You could easily put an Intelligence-boosting Charm in Investigation. Socialize, meanwhile, grants Mastery of Small Manners, which grants a bonus Appearance dot. That's definitely something that could serve as the foundation of boosting Appearance in general. The themes of the game say that Solars are A Number One, the Dukes of Creation, and so the rules follow. Anything trying to muscle in on this territory by other Exalted dooms said Exalted to languish in the shadows of greatness. Find another way.<br /> <br /> And speaking of muscling in, apparently there was some artificial mandate to make Lunars have greater might-oriented Charms than Solars in 2e. That's why Thunder's Might and Ten Ox Meditation didn't show up. This, however, is pretty much in the same corner as Lunars not having scene long defenses and having to rely on those damned gatekeeper Charms - a bad idea. We've been assured that the mistake won't be repeated (and in any case, Solars have a much easier time getting and using Unconquerable Might from DotFA anyway, assuming you're using any material from Lords of Creation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Alchemicals at that level - okay? So a freshly tattooed Lunar with Intelligence 5 (+3 practically everything) straight out of chargen is <i>only</i> as intelligent as a high-essence Alchemical who's had intelligence-boosting charms physically installed and... umm... uh... </div> </div> </div>Trying to cite a specialty as applying to practically everything? Really? This is what you're doing?<br /> <br /> The well didn't run dry for your advocacy. It never had water in it at all in the first place. You're trying to irrigate with dry sand.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:41:01-07:00","id":102713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102678#post102678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so you find it and eat its heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Because the thing about monsters is... They exist only to test the will of the hero who's strong enough to go against them. If you're presenting Lunars as monsters, you're acknowledging that at some point, something with strong enough will, sharp enough wits, skilled enough arm, will kill them and feast upon their hearts. and tradinionally, the role of the monster-slayer... Is that of a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-31-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:48:57-07:00","id":102722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102688#post102688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong. Dice caps are based on something. If we're ignoring the origin of dice cap, your assumptions get knocked off at the knees... or would, if they could stand. Solars draw off of their capability and skill, not just the latter. That's what their dice cap of Attribute + Ability means. Lunars don't draw off their skill. That's what their dice cap means. This is not a matter up for discussion, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eesh, the claws are coming out now, aren't they? Yes, they mean something, but what do they mean? I keep saying Lunar powers aren't based on skill. I keep saying there's a difference between potential and application and that even if a Lunar is stronger than a Solar, the Solar can still apply his strength through martial arts and achieve a better result. What are you actually disagreeing with me about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102688#post102688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Solars get both avenues. I doubt that Increasing Strength Exercise is the only Charm of its kind. You could easily put an Intelligence-boosting Charm in Investigation. Socialize, meanwhile, grants Mastery of Small Manners, which grants a bonus Appearance dot. That's definitely something that could serve as the foundation of boosting Appearance in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about inventing new charms for Solars to give them Lunar-like abilities, great. What should I call that? Golden Lunars? As long as you're homebrewing, you might as well just give Lunars some more dice-boosting charms. It works both ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102688#post102688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The themes of the game say that Solars are A Number One, the Dukes of Creation, and so the rules follow. Anything trying to muscle in on this territory by other Exalted dooms said Exalted to languish in the shadows of greatness. Find another way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's telling that you're explicitly framing your argument in terms of territorialism now (edit: which, for the record, is Lunar territory). The themes of Solars are justice, virtue and unequalled excellence in the application of power and skill. But they're not the best at <i>everything</i> in the game and never have been. They're not the best at manipulating fate or practicing martial arts. They're not the best at shapeshifting. They're not the best when it comes to raw attributes like intelligence and charisma. This is not a subject for argument. They're just <i>not.</i> It's in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102688#post102688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to cite a specialty as applying to practically everything? Really? This is what you're doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Comparing an Essence 5 Alchemical to an Essence 3 Lunar? Ignoring the fact that a Lunar at the same level can raise his Intelligence higher than 5? Is that what you're doing? (Yes, it is what you're doing.)<br /> <br /> For that matter, aren't you overlooking something? Namely, that an Essence 5 Alchemical can only have Intelligence 8 <i>as long as</i> that charm remains physically installed? It doesn't represent the Alchemical's innate intelligence. It's more like wearing an artifact that grants you additional intelligence, and anyone can play that game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102688#post102688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The well didn't run dry for your advocacy. It never had water in it at all in the first place. You're trying to irrigate with dry sand.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I've been doing is quoting to you straight from the core rulebook. You've been arguing with the books, arguing with the dictionary, arguing with yourself, because you're trying to argue for something that goes against the basic mechanics and themes of the game. Yes, intelligence <i>does </i>mean intelligence. And yes, Lunars <i>do</i> have more raw intelligence than Solars. If you feel that threatens your concept of Solars, maybe you should get a new concept of Solars. I'm sorry but that's just how it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-01-2014, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:10:53-07:00","id":102741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102722#post102722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eesh, the claws are coming out now, aren't they? Yes, they mean something, but what do they mean? I keep saying Lunar powers aren't based on skill. I keep saying there's a difference between potential and application and that even if a Lunar is stronger than a Solar, the Solar can still apply his strength through martial arts and achieve a better result. What are you actually disagreeing with me about?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've been going round and round with the same flat-out-wrong argument for so long, that yes, normally calm people will get their jimmies rustled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we're talking about inventing new charms for Solars to give them Lunar-like abilities, great. What should I call that? Golden Lunars? As long as you're homebrewing, you might as well just give Lunars more dice-boosting charms. It works both ways. </div> </div> </div>They aren't Lunar-like. Increasing Strength Exercise was published before the writing started on Lunars 1e. The burden of breaking away from Solar design schema is on the Lunars, not the Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's telling that you're framing your argument in terms of territorialism now, and feeling territory threatened by someone else. The themes of Solars are justice, virtue and unequalled excellence in the application of power and skill. But they're not the best at everything in the game and never have been. They're not the best at manipulating fate or practicing martial arts. They're not the bet at shapeshifting. They're not the best when it comes to raw attributes like intelligence and charisma. This is not a subject for argument. They're just <i>not.</i> It's in the book. </div> </div> </div>You're practically ramming your head into a brick wall here. The official word on this is that &quot;extreme Attribute&quot; cannot be meaningfully distinguished from &quot;extreme&quot;, which is the corner the Solars occupy. There;s no saving the Silver Solar Charms. But then, they mostly just fill the Lunar Charm set up with more Charms than what really need to be there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I've been doing is quoting to you straight from the core rulebook. You've been arguing with the books, arguing with the dictionary, arguing with yourself, because you're trying to argue for something that goes against the basic mechanics and themes of the game. You're running on fumes. Yes, intelligence <i>does </i>mean intelligence. And yes, Lunars <i>do</i> have more raw intelligence than Solars. If you feel that threatens your concept of Solars, maybe you should get a new concept of Solars. I'm sorry but that's just how it is. </div> </div> </div>I think we're done here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:16:31-07:00","id":102746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102741#post102741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've been going round and round with the same flat-out-wrong argument for so long, that yes, normally calm people will get their jimmies rustled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flat-out wrong arguments like &quot;Intelligence doesn't mean intelligence,&quot; &quot;Monstrous doesn't mean highly capable,&quot; etc. etc. etc.? There is nothing to your arguments so far except straightforward denial of the definitions of various concepts used in the game, as they are explained in the core rulebook and in other books. Sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102741#post102741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't Lunar-like. Increasing Strength Exercise was published before the writing started on Lunars 1e. The burden of breaking away from Solar design schema is on the Lunars, not the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>One charm does not define a charm tree or an Exalt type. And you can't simply say the burden is on me to prove my opinion because book B was published after book A. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:51:14-07:00","id":102781,"title":"","content":"Perhaps we should start a new thread since we have long since stopped talking about philosophy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T22:15:30-07:00","id":103172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/97188-are-lunars-the-best-philosophers-in-creation?p=102713#post102713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly! Because the thing about monsters is... They exist only to test the will of the hero who's strong enough to go against them. If you're presenting Lunars as monsters, you're acknowledging that at some point, something with strong enough will, sharp enough wits, skilled enough arm, will kill them and feast upon their hearts. and tradinionally, the role of the monster-slayer... Is that of a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm, very clever.<br /> <br /> But monsters exist with or without heroes to slay them. In my experience, it's more often the case that there are no heroes at all, only monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-01-2014, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}